1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ='''Ingeborg Sigvidsdotter Ribbing'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Sigvid Sigvidsson "Rövaren" Ribbing and Märta Ulfsdotter Hjorthufvud 
2 CONT * Birth:	cirka 1360
2 CONT * Death:	after circa 1413
2 CONT * Sister to Arvid Sigvidsson Ribbing och Peter Sigvidsson Ribbing 
2 CONT * Half sister to Ingegerd Knutsdotter (Bengt Hafridssons ätt); Katarina Knutsdotter (Bengt Hafridssons ätt) och Ingrid Knutsdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children of Sigvid Sigvidsson "Rövaren" Ribbing and Märta Ulfsdotter Hjorthufvud=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Peder''', à Vapn; Svea Rikes Råd; Was childless and in 1402 went with his wife to the holy tomb, but they were to die on the road. In 1375, as a pledge, the Second Council of Sweden sometimes confirmed a King Albrecht's Chart
2 CONC er; likewise in 1376 the King's letter to the dioceses in the kingdom stated: shall finally give Hamneryd (two farms in Ås) and Flateryds mill in Wadsbo district, which all he inherited from his nephew Arvid Ribbing, to Wadstena m
2 CONC onastery, according to a written record written in 1518, which Arvid Skeff, who was Ingeborgs, Arvid Ribbing 's wife Redesven, must have given Peder Ribbing is called by Catharina Knutsdotter (Griphufvud), in  his confirmation let
2 CONC ter for Wadstena monastery brother (half-brother). - Married 1360 to Christina Ulfsdotter; daughter of Riddaren, Riks-Råd and Lagmannen Ulfo Abjörnsson (Sparre, No. 7), to Tofta, with his 1st wife, Margaretha Sunesdotter (Bååt, No
2 CONC . 3). 
2 CONT * '''Arvid'''  (son of Sigvid Ribbing, Tab. 2), à Vapn; Lived in 1390. - Married 1st with Ingeborg Magnusdotter, of the old Stureätten, in her 2nd marriage; daughter of the Knight and Riks-Råd Magnus Amundsson (Sture) and widow of
2 CONC  Ulf Nilsson, à Vapn, of whom she received as a morning present Hamneryd and Sundra farm and mill, but with whom she had no children: - 2nd with Brita Pehrsdotter; daughter of the Knight Pehr Sture. Sons: Arvid; Drowned unmarried 
2 CONC in Upland &Peder; Svea Rikes Råd.
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg''' Married Peter Andersson Prika, i Möne 
2 CONT * '''Bengt'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Peter Andersson Prika (stjärna)''' son of Anders Prika i Gällstad
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Peter Andersson Prika (stjärna) =
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ingegerd (Pedersdotter) Prika''' Birth:	1380 in Gällstad, Västergötland & died before 1438, in Västergötland, Sverige (Sweden). Married Arvid Jönsson (Sparre över Stjärna). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prika Prika, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Peter Prika's widow Ingeborg Sigvidsdotter seals a document in Lödöse on February 10, 1413, with the family Ribbing's three downward leaflets when she sells her seat Torpa , and a number of other farms to the national council A
2 CONC lgot Magnusson ( Three Roses to Horshaga . [ 10 ]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ingeborg Sigvidsdotter, widow of Peter Prika, sells to Tor Algot Magnusson his Torpa farm, seven farms in Flundrevalla, one mill and two mill streams in Fors sn, one mill stream in "Syundafors" and farms in Anstorp (?; Austhensto
2 CONC rpp) in Rommeleds sn, Flounder hd, Gammanstorp, Huvudnäs (Hughanæs) in Vassenda sn, Väne hd, Tillhagen in Bolstad sn, Lånstorp (in Bolstad socken) and "Vluidhathorpp" in Grinstads sn on Dal, three farms in Björketorp in Surteby sn
2 CONC  and one in Kitten in Kitten sn, Mark's hd."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =='''SDHK No:''' [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/person?Namn=Ingeborg+Sigvidsdotter+&AvanceradSok=True&PageSize=20&page=1&postid=sdhk_13678&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab''' 13678''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating: 1390 February 2 * Place of issue:  Öresten''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingeborg Sigvidsdotter sells and leases several farms in Vista district and in Åse district to Nils Svarte Skåning. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Post-medieval transcripts:  B 16 fol. 404v, no. 36, RA 0202 (see transcripts of B 16 texts, DK)
2 CONT
2 CONT =='''SDHK no:''' [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&SDHK=17958&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaRegest=true&Efterm
2 CONC edeltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_17958&tab=post#tab '''17958'''] 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''February 10, 1413,  Place of issue: Solder''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingeborg Sigvidsdotter, widow of Peter Prika , sells to rd Algot Magnusson his manor Torpa, seven farms in Flundrevalla, a mill and two mill streams in Fors sn, a mill stream in "Syundafors" and farms in Anstorp (?; Austhenstorpp)
2 CONC  in Rommeleds sn, Flundre hd, Gammanstorp, Huvudnäs (Hughanæs) in Vassända sn, Väne hd, Tillhagen in Bolstads sn, Lånstorp (in Bolstads parish) and "Vluidhathorpp" in Grinstads sn on Dal, three farms in Björketorp in Surteby sn an
2 CONC d one in Kattunge in Kattunge sn, Marks hd.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SEAL''' :No. 1 Three downward-facing lake leaves with rewrite: ingeborgh sivitsdot .; No. 2 Bishop Brynolfs; No. 3 Gustav Magnussons (cf. SDHK No. 15552 , seal No. 2); No. 4 Torsten Simonssons (cf. SDHK no. 15541 , seal no. 4) 
2 CONC [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/17958.pdf '''SD 1678 see pdf of print with over. in Dalslands Diplomatarium no. 95''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No:'''  [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&Innehall=%22prika%22&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaRegest=tru
2 CONC e&EftermedeltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=4&postid=sdhk_13686&tab=post#tab' 13686]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating1390 February 13'''
2 CONT * Place of issue: Open 
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Nilsson and his wife Elin "Deyia" pledge to Tove Benosson's estate in Nittorp (s parish, Kinds district) for 30 marks of money in oxen and cows to be handed over next Johannesdag (midsummer).
2 CONT '''As the issuers do not have a seal, the honest and well-to-do men ask Peter Ribbing, Peter Prika, Jöns Bengtsson and Magnus Nilsson to seal.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000004661569157?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000186037497964 '''Original Copy of the document SDHK No. 13686.''']  Original:  or. perg. RA 0101. Post-medieval transcripts:  Brocman: Mis
2 CONC c. 4:67; Hadorph: III, E 80 fol. 65 no. 66; Peringskiöld: E 68 no. 77 (reg, Stenhag.), 66 (Wennæs.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://runeberg.org/anrep/3/0375.html '''Von Nackreij - Skytte, Volume 3, page 371''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sigvid Ribbing in Scania;''' Called in Anna Bülow's Notice of Old Family Seved Ribbing; Where a well-born lord of Scania, who lived in 1345, who may have come from Norway in 1335; Referred to as a stern and hard man; Considered
2 CONC  the ancestor of all the Ribbings in Sweden, and with him Peringsköld begins his hand written pedigrees of the Ribbing family. - Married to Märta Ulfsdotter (Hjorthufvud), in her 1st marriage, b. In the year 1320; Was around 1353—
2 CONC 1363 a strict Adulterer for Queen Margaretha in her younger years; † in Norway and 
2 CONT buried there; daughter of Riddaren and Svea Rikes Råd  and Lagmannen i Nerike Ulf Gudmarsson  (Hjorthufvud or Folkunge), to Ulfåsa, who first carried in the weapon a deer head with a neck, then his the mothers or Folkungevapnet, a
2 CONC  lion, with Brigitta Birgersdotter or Sancta Brita (see Brahe, No. 1) and remarried with the Knight Knut Algotsson to Hammarö, of the old Grip- or Griphufvudslägten. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.rotter.se/faktabanken/rotterarkivet/efterlysningar/1217-efterlysningar-1000-1099 Online Magazine RÖTTER]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Christina Håkansdotter, daughter of Håkan Karlsson-Tun, de 1478, owned Attorp in Sämns sn married to Ingrid Knutsdotter (chevron over star). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingrid dtr to Knut Arvidsson. chevron over star. Died 1459. District Chief. Knut is called a gunsmith in letter 1438 and was district chief in Kind 1438-58. In 1453, he sold his farm Smedjeby on Öland, which he got from his uncle,
2 CONC  Mr. Vernike. Married to Kerstin Bengtsdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut son of Arvid Jönsson. chevron. Died about 1438. District chief. Arvid Jönsson was district chief in Ås hd 1401-15 and in Kinds hd 1421-34. He lived at Möne in Ås hd and then at Intorp in Kinds hd. Married before 1416 withInge
2 CONC borgPetersdotter-Prika.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arvid son of Jöns Bengtsson. chevron. Died after 1414. Gunsmith, District Chief. Jöns Bengtsson owned Ryslatorp (Retstorp) in Gällstads sn Kinds hd and was district chief in Kind 1397-1412. Jöns and his son Arvid testify in 1409 w
2 CONC hen Abraham Brodersson buys a farm in Håksviks sn and in 1412 he testifies that Märta Larsdotter inherited from Peter Prika.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kerstin dtr to Bengt Turesson. chevron over leaves. Died after 1422. Gunman. In 1403, Bengt Turesson bought the farm Arvidstorp in Fagereds sn from Jösse But, which is certified by Peter Djekn, bailiff at Varberg. The same year, B
2 CONC engt seals together with Gunnar and Jösse Gylta when Jöns Påvelsson and Ingegerd Arvidsdotter sell farms in Valinge. In 1405, Bengt, together with Jöns Påvelsson, Gunnar Gylta and Gamol Thorisson, witnessed Ås monastery certify Gu
2 CONC dhem monastery's sales of goods in Denmark. In 1420, Bengt witnesses the succession between Gunnar Gylta and Lars Pik. Married to Märta Gunnarsdotter-Gylta. Ingeborgdtr to Peter Prika. Died before 1413. Gunman. Peter Prika was kno
2 CONC wn in Oppestens in Kinds hd 1397 later in Möne sn Ås hd. Married toIngeborgSigvidsdotter-Ribbing. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Märta dtr to Gunnar Nilsson-Gylta. Died before 1429. In 1409, Gunnar and his brother Björn hold the handle of Bengt Arvidsson's morning present toIngeborgLarsdotter. In 1416 Gudmund Sigmundsson ceded a farm in Ås to Gunnar Gylta. 
2 CONC In 1416, Gunnar and his brother Jösse inherit from their brothers Björn and Magnus. The inheritance included Gälared where Gunnar is said to have lived. Through his marriage, he came into possession of Påtorp in Fristads sn, which
2 CONC  later became Gylta's manor. In 1420, Gunnar and Lars Pik inherit from Katarina Karlsdotter, Gunnar's mother-in-law. Married to Märta Olofsdotter. Gunnar son of Nils Gylta. Nils Gylta was probably married to a sister of Peter Prik
2 CONC a. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingeborgdtr to Sigvid Magnusson-Ribbing. In 1351, Sigvid and his brother Assar pledge a debt. Sigge Pettersson-Djekn. sloping beam with animal heads. Died after 1349. Sigge Djekn is first mentioned in 1323 when he buys his wife's 
2 CONC share in Vinstorp Böne sn from Haldor Magnusson, which is later inherited by his daughter married to Karl Ingemundsson. 1331 Ulf Kärling declares that he is in charge of the administration of his sister, 11) Peder Håkansson Hand. 
2 CONC Died after 1488. Gunman. Peder Håkansson is mentioned in a document dated Länghem 1488 together with his brother-in-law, Councilor Arvid Knutsson Drake. Peder is the ancestor of the noble family Drake of Hagelsrum. The weapon hand
2 CONC  appears a few generations earlier in an Atte Pedersson, known in Köping 1400. Possibly there is a connection as the family's oldest manors are called Attetorp, Attarp.  12) Gustav Olsson (Capricorn). Olof Jönsson (Capricorn). Die
2 CONC d after 1441. Gunman, District Chief. Olof Jönsson owned Erikstad in Vittaryds sn Sunnerbo hd and he was district chief in Sunnerbo. Married to Estrid Knutsdotter-Körning. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Olof son of Jöns Skytte. Squire. Jöns Skytte owned Ekornatorp in Berga sn and Erikstad in Vittaryd sn in Sunnerbo hd. Married to Kristina. - Mother: Katarina Västensdotter.
2 CONT
