1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Margaret of Scotland (28 February 1261–9 April 1283) (Old Norse:Margrét Alexandersdóttir; modern Norwegian: Margrete Alexandersdotter Scottish Gaelic: Maighread Nic Rìgh Alasdair) was queen of Norway, married to Ki
2 CONC ng Eirik II of Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_of_Scotland_%28Queen_of_Norway%29
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born at Windsor Castle, the daughter of King Alexander III of Scotland and his first wife, Margaret of England. She married Eirik in Bergen in 1281.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in Tønsberg, presumably during or shortly after giving birth to Margaret, who became (arguably) queen regnant of the Kingdom of Scotland in 1286. The date of her death is given as 9 April 1283 in the Gesta Annalia, but th
2 CONC e Chronicle of Lanercost states her death as 27/28 February 1283. She was buried in the old cathedral of Bergen. This cathedral was demolished in 1531, the site, in present day Bergenhus Fortress, is marked by a memorial.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried ~ The old cathedral was demolished in 1531. The site, in present day Bergenhus Fortress, is marked by a memorial.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT The book, 'Windsor Castle', by Edward Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT The book, 'The Oxford History of the British Monarchy'
2 CONT
2 CONT The book, 'Scotland, A Concise History'
2 CONT
2 CONT The book, 'Scotland's Story' 
