2 CONT =[https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bogislav_IX Bogislaw IX, Duke of Pomerania, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bogislaw IX (Polish: Bogusław IX; 1407/1410 – 7 December 1446) was a duke of Pomerania in Pomerania-Stolp, whose residence was Stargard.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bogislaw was the son of Bogislaw VIII, Duke of Pomerania, and Sophia of Holstein. On June 24, 1432 he married Maria of Masovia, daughter of Siemowit IV, Duke of Masovia and Alexandra of Lithuania. They had two daughters, Sophia, w
2 CONC ho married Eric II, Duke of Pomerania, and Alexandra.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Polish–Teutonic War (1431–1435), Bogislaw opposed the Teutonic Knights and supported the Kingdom of Poland. He was later involved in struggles related to Pomeranian bishops.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bogislaw was succeeded by Eric of Pomerania.
