1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT "Philippa of England (4 June 1394 – 7 January 1430), also known as Philippa of Lancaster and anachronistically as Philippa Plantagenet, was the Queen of Denmark, Sweden and Norway from 1406 to 1430. She was the consort to Eric of 
2 CONC Pomerania, who ruled the three kingdoms. Queen Philippa served as the de facto regent of Sweden in 1420 and the regent of Denmark and Norway from 1423 to 1425."
2 CONT
2 CONT =================================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Links:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippa_of_England
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/philippa-of-england/Philippa_of_England_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/8079895/philippa
2 CONT
2 CONT https://royalfamilytree.uk/13940604_queen_of_denmark_norway_and_sweden_philippa_of_engl.html
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/GGHN-VCK/philippa-of-lancaster-%2C-queen-of-denmark-1394-1430
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10187.htm#i101870
2 CONT
2 CONT =================================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations / Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), pages 126-127. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S1850] Medieval Lands: A Prosopography of Medieval European Noble and Royal Families, Charles Cawley, (http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/), England, Kings 1066-1603 [accessed 28 Jun 2006].
2 CONT
