1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sancha,_Lady_of_Alenquer
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Born a princess, the daughter of King Sancho I of Portugal; sister of Blessed Mafilda and Saint Theresa of Portugal. She devoted herself to charity, supported the Franciscans and Dominicans in Portugal including helping Franciscan
2 CONC  missionaries en route to Morocco. Founded a Cistercian monastery in Coimbra, Portugal where she spent the rest of her life in a cell there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Canonized as Saint Sancha of Portugal 10 May 1705 by Pope Clement XI (cultus confirmation)
2 CONT
2 CONT MLA Citation
2 CONT
