1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Heinrich I Margrave of Brandenburg-Stendal, "ohne Land"=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Markgraf Johann von Brandenburg, I and Markgrafin Brigitte von Sachsen, Markgräfin von Brandenburg 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRANDENBURG,%20PRUSSIA.htm#JohannIdied12661267 Project MedLands, Prussia, Brandenburg]
2 CONT
2 CONT HEINRICH [I] von Brandenburg "ohne Land" (1260-14 Feb 1318). The Cronica Principum Saxonie names (in order) "Albertum, Hermannum et Henricum" as sons of "Iohannes" and his second wife Jutta[336]. The Annales Lubicenses names "Agne
2 CONC tem filiam marchionis de Brandenborch, sororis Ottonis marchionis cum thelo et Hinrici marchionis dicti ane land"[337]. "Otto…Brandenburg et de Landesberg marchio" granted Schloß Querfurt to the bishop of Brandenburg, with the con
2 CONC sent of "fratris nostri Hinrici…patruelium nostrorum Johannis et Wolmari, de Brandenburg et de Landesberg Marchionum", by charter dated 10 Jan 1305[338]. m ([Nov 1298/19 May 1303], Papal dispensation Anagni 19 May 1303) as her sec
2 CONC ond husband, AGNES von Bayern, widow of HEINRICH Landgraf von Hessen, daughter of LUDWIG II "der Strenge" Duke of Bavaria, Pfalzgraf bei Rhein & his third wife Mechtild von Habsburg ([1276/78]-22 Jul 1345). Her origin is confirmed
2 CONC  by the charter dated 21 Aug 1323 under which "Ludowicus…Romanorum Rex" granted rights to "Sophie…sororis nostre Agnetis, relicte quondam Henrici Marchionis Brandenburgensis, filie"[339]. Burchard Archbishop of Magdeburg agreed an
2 CONC  alliance with “Agn der Margreuinen von Brandenborch unde tu Landesberch”, with the consent of “hertoghen Hinrike von Brunswik erem swaghere”, by charter dated 16 Apr 1318[340]. Markgraf Heinrich & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1) '''''JUTTA''''' ([1299/1306]-[15 Jul 1325/early Feb 1327]). Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by the charter dated 16 Apr 1318 under which Burchard Archbishop of Magdeburg agreed an alliance with “Agn der Margreuinen v
2 CONC on Brandenborch unde tu Landesberch” with the consent of “hertoghen Hinrike von Brunswik erem swaghere”[341]. m (before 16 Apr 1318) as his first wife, HEINRICH von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen, son of HEINRICH I Herzog von Braunschwe
2 CONC ig und Lüneburg in Grubenhagen und Salzderhelden & his wife Agnes von Meissen ([1289]-[10 Apr/8 Jun] 1351, bur Grubenhagen). He succeeded his father in 1322 as HEINRICH II "der Junge" Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2) '''''SOPHIE''''' (1300-[1356]). "Ludowicus…Romanorum Rex" granted rights to "Sophie…sororis nostre Agnetis, relicte quondam Henrici Marchionis Brandenburgensis, filie" by charter dated 21 Aug 1323[342]. m MAGNUS I Herzog von 
2 CONC Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Göttingen, son of ALBRECHT II "der Fette/der Feiste" Herzog von Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Göttingen und Braunschweig & his wife Richza von Werle ([1304]-[15 Jun/15 Aug] 1369, bur Lüneburg St Michael
2 CONC is). 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3) '''''MARGARETE''''' (1301-31 Mar 1347, bur Weissenfels St Klara). Abbess of St Klara at Weissenfels.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 4)  '''''HEINRICH von Brandenburg''''' ([1302/10]-early Jul 1320, bur Prenzlau Marienkirche). 
2 CONT
