2 CONT
2 CONT Father:	John I, Margrave of Brandenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother:	Jutta of Saxony
2 CONT
2 CONT Margrave Henry I (nicknamed Henry Lackland; 21 March 1256 – 14 February 1318) was a member of the House of Ascania and Margrave of Brandenburg-Stendal and Landsberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Marriage and issue==
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was married to Agnes, the daughter of Duke Louis II "the Strict" of Bavaria and widow of Landgrave Henry the Younger of Hesse. Henry and Agnes had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Henry II, Margrave of Brandenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT *Sophia (1300-1356), married Duke Magnus I of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel
2 CONT
2 CONT *Judith, married in 1318 to Duke Henry II of Brunswick-Grubenhagen
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_I,_Margrave_of_Brandenburg-Stendal Wikipedia Henry I Margrave of Brandenburg]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Life==
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was a son of Margrave John I of Brandenburg and his third wife, Jutta, the daughter of Duke Albert I of Saxony. The origin of his nickname "Lackland" is not known. Henry was more than fifteen years younger than his brothers 
2 CONC John II, Otto IV "with the arrow" and Conrad I and was therefore likely to be excluded from governing when his brothers inherited the Margraviate.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was not until 1294 he began to participate in the government of the country. When he did, he received — according to an excerpt from the Bohemian chronicler Přibík Pulkava — Delitzsch as his seat. Delitzsch was located in the M
2 CONC argraviate of Landsberg, which Margrave Albert II of Meissen had sold to the Margraves of Brandenburg. From then on, Henry used the title of Margrave of Landsberg in addition to Margrave of Brandenburg in almost all documents. As 
2 CONC Margrave of Landsberg, he fought several feuds with neighbouring princes. He was excommunicated by archbishop Burchard II of Magdeburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1311, Henry lost a feud to Duke Rudolf I of Saxony and had to hand over the County Palatine of Saxony with the castles Grillenberg Castle in Sangerhausen and Raspenburg Castle in Rastenberg to Rudolf I. He also lost a feud to M
2 CONC argrave Dietrich IV of Lusatia.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Emperor Henry VII, Henry's nephew Margrave Waldemar proposed to elect Henry I as King of the Romans. Henry I appears to have declined the proposal, and his promised by deed to vote for Duke Frederick the Fair or his brother 
2 CONC Leopold I. However, in the end, Henry voted for Duke Louis IV of Bavaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry died on 14 February 1318 at the age of 61 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
