2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT Otto V, Margrave of Brandenburg-Salzwedel
2 CONT Born	c. 1246
2 CONT Died	1298
2 CONT Noble family	House of Ascania
2 CONT Spouse(s)	Judith of Henneberg-Coburg
2 CONT Father	Otto III
2 CONT Mother	Beatrice of Bohemia
2 CONT Margrave Otto V of Brandenburg-Salzwedel (c. 1246 – 1298), nicknamed Otto the Tall, was a son of Margrave Otto III and co-ruler of Brandenburg with his cousin, Margrave Otto IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto V spent many years in Prague, at the court of his maternal uncle King Ottokar II of Bohemia. When Ottokar died in battle in 1278, Otto V became the regent for Ottokar's son and heir Wenceslaus II, who was only seven years old
2 CONC  when his father died. As regent, Otto V had to deal with the machinations of Ottokar's widow Kunigunda of Slavonia and with factions of powerful noblemen. Bohemian chroniclers describe Otto's persistent rigour and that Wenceslaus
2 CONC  was forced to give up his claims on Upper Lusatia before he could start reigning himself. When Wenceslaus had taken over, he and Otto V were still on good terms, and Wenceslaus took measures against the strong influence of the gr
2 CONC oup around his mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto V also persistently defended his claims on Pomerania against Polish counter-claims.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT He married with Judith of Henneberg-Coburg, a daughter of Count Herman I of Henneberg. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda (c. 1270 – before 1 June 1298), the second wife of Henry IV Probus, Duke of Wrocław and High Duke of Poland
2 CONT Herman (c. 1275 – 1 February 1308), his successor
2 CONT Otto (died 1307)
2 CONT Kunigunde (died 1317), never married
2 CONT Beatrix (d. c. 1316), married Bolko I the Strict, Duke of Świdnica in 1284
2 CONT Judith (also known as Jutta; died: 9 May 1328), married Rudolph I, Duke of Saxe-Wittenberg in 1303
2 CONT Albert (before 1283 – c. 1296)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Wikipedia
2 CONT Otto V, Markgraf von Brandenburg is my/our 22nd great grandfather.
2 CONT Janet Milburn 10/23/23
