1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *  Countess Elisabeth of Henneberg, daughter of Berthold VII, Count of Henneberg-Schleusingen, before 3 March 1333. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Their children were:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.'''Frederick V, Burgrave of Nuremberg''' (before 3 March 1333 – 21 January 1398). 2.Margarete (died 1377), married in 1359, Landshut, to Duke Stephen II, Duke of Bavaria. 3.Elisabeth (died ca 1383), married 1360, to Ulrich, Co
2 CONC unt of Schaunberg. 4.Anna (died 1383), Abbess of Birkenfeld and of Himmelkron. 5.Adelheid, a nun in Birkenfeld from 1361 to 1370.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAVARIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#JohannIIdied1357 Project MedLands, BAVARIAN NOBILITY]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''JOHANN''' (-7 Oct 1357, bur Heilsbronn).  His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 27 Jan 1356 under which [his brother] Berthold Bishop of Eichstätt confirmed an agreement between “Herzog Albrechten von Osterrich and “G
2 CONC raf Albrechtz dem Eltern von Werdenberg und Graf Albrechten seinem Sun und unserr...Swester Agnesen, desselben grafen Albrechts des Jungen Wirtinne und unsern...brudern Johansen und Albrechten Burggrafen ze Nurnberg”[1686].  Canon
2 CONC  at Würzburg cathedral 1319.  He succeeded his father in 1332 as JOHANN II Burggraf von Nürnberg.  In 1332, Emperor Ludwig IV granted the town of Nürnberg freedom from imposts and dues of many kinds in 70 places, mainly in norther
2 CONC n Germany[1687].  Vogt von Heilsbronn 1333.  Herr zu Plassenburg und Pfandherr zu Kulmbach 1338.  He ruled Nürnberg jointly with his brother Johann after an agreement 10 Oct 1341.  Pfleger und Hauptmann der Mark Brandenburg 1346. 
2 CONC  '''married (before 3 Mar 1333) ELISABETH von Henneberg, daughter of BERTHOLD [IV] Graf von Henneberg-Schleusingen & his first wife Adelheid von Hessen (-[6 Dec 1377/30 May 1391]).'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann II & his wife ELISABETH von Henneberg had five children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* a)         '''FRIEDRICH'''  (before 3 Mar 1333-Plassenburg 21 Jan 1398, bur Heilsbronn).  '''He succeeded his father in 1357 as joint FRIEDRICH V Burggraf von Nürnberg, ruling jointly with his uncle Albrecht until the latte
2 CONC r's death in 1361.  Recognised as Reichsfürst at Nürnberg 17 Mar 1363.''' 
2 CONT >>>>>* b)         '''MARGARETA'''  (-19 Sep 1377).  The Chronicle of Matthias Nueweburgensis records that "Stephani ducis Bavarie" married "filiam burggravii de Nürenberg" after the death of his first wife[1688].  The necrology of
2 CONC  Seligenthal records the death "XIII Kal Oct 1377" of "nobilis domina Margareta ducissa Bawarie, filia domini purggrafii de Nurenperga"[1689].  '''married  (Landshut 14 Feb 1359) as his second wife, STEFAN II "mit der Hafte" Duke 
2 CONC of Bavaria, son of Emperor LUDWIG IV "der Bayer" King of Germany, Duke of Bavaria, Pfalzgraf bei Rhein & his first wife Beatrix von Schweidnitz [Piast] (Autumn 1319-Landshut 19 May 1375, bur Munich Unsere Liebe Frau).  Duke of Bav
2 CONC aria in Upper Bavaria 1363.''' 
2 CONT >>>>>* c)         ELISABETH (-[1383], bur Kloster Wilhering).  '''married  ([9 Feb 1353, before 5 Apr 1360) ULRICH Graf von Schaunberg, son of --- (-Schaunberg 6 Mar 1373).''' 
2 CONT >>>>>* d)         ANNA (-27 Jul 1383, bur Himmelskron).  Abbess of Birkenfeld 1359/60.  Abbess of Himmelskron 1370/83. 
2 CONT >>>>>* e)         '''ADELHEID''' .  1361/70.  Nun in Birkenfeld. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
