2 CONT
2 CONT * Svenska sigiller från medeltiden 
2 CONT * Author / Editor: Hildebrand, Bror Emil ; Hildebrand, Bror Emil
2 CONT * Publishing place: Stockholm | Year of publication: 1862 - 67 | Publishing house: Akad. förlag 
2 CONT * Call number: 2 Herald. 27 h-1 
2 CONT * Series: Svenska sigiller från medeltiden 
2 CONT * Permalink: http://mdz-nbn-resolving.de/urn:nbn:de:bvb:12-
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcripts:  Peringskiöld: E 60 fol. 147; Örnhielm: IX pp. 638
2 CONT * About Erengisle Sunesson (boat), titular earl of the Orkney Islands, and his third wife Ingeborg Magnusdotter (Ulvåsaätten) see ÄSF I, p. 92. About Erengisle's nephews Karl Ulfsson and Kristina Ulfsdotter till Fågelvik (Sparre a
2 CONC v Tofta) see ÄSF I, p. 87 f.
2 CONT * For the listed properties in Ålems, Mönsterås and Högsby parishes, see DMS, Småland 4: 2.
2 CONT * About Västramark, a border area in the western part of Handbörds district, see DMS, aa, p. 26.
2 CONT * On Hammarby Fjarding as evidence of an early division into Fjärding in Högsby parish, see DMS, aa, p. 79.
2 CONT * Erengisle Sunesson seems to have originally drawn up the will only for himself and only later brought in his wife, which is shown by the fact that Mrs. Ingeborg's name was added as well as by the pronouns written in rasur in the
2 CONC  plural ('vi', 'vår' etc.) which replace singular forms ( see text notes below).
2 CONT * Ang. Åsevad see Festskrift till Harry Ståhl, 1985, p. 320.
2 CONT * Gallèn, Jarl (1957). Wernstedt Folke . ed. Ulvåsaätten . Older Swedish families of salvation: genealogies. Bd 1. H. 1. Stockholm: Riddarhusdirektionen. p. 92. - 
2 CONT * Raneke, Jan. Swedish medieval weapons
2 CONT * Äldre Svenska Frälseätter I: 1, sid 92 b
2 CONT
