1 NAME Peter "Dominius" /Israelsson/
2 GIVN Peter "Dominius"
2 SURN Israelsson
2 _MARNM Israelsson
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1240
2 PLAC Skederid Finsta
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Sweden
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1296
2 PLAC Sverige
2 ADDR
3 STAE Uppland
3 CTRY Sverige
1 OCCU Riddare, riddare, lagman i Tiundaland, Uppland, sammanställde Upplandslagen, Dominus
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Äldre svenska frälsesläkter I:1 s. 34-38.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Israel, stamfar Finsta 
2 CONT * Knight Peter Israelsson, who is mentioned in records from years 1269-74
2 CONT * Peter Israelsson was well traveled and visited, among other things. Jerusalem. He had two sons, Birger and Israel. Birger's son was in turn the father of Saint Birgitta - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&i
2 CONC d=6000000003820985279&photo_id=6000000090552231959&position=0
2 CONT * Peter Israelsson is called Dominus 1269 and died June 29, 1280; about his pilgrimage see above. '''He married  a daughter of Birger Skänkare, who is said to have carried two wings in the weapon (Rosman).''' Sons of them were the
2 CONC  upland batsman, the national council and the knight Birger Petersson and Israel Petersson, who became cannibal in Uppsala in 1295 and in 1299 succeeded his cousin Andreas Andreæ (And) as a court judge there. Mr. Israel was dead o
2 CONC n 24 Nov 1302. His anniversary was celebrated in Uppsala Cathedral together with his cousin Karl Erlandssons (see below) on 12 Aug, which was probably Israel's day of death. Teamman Birger Petersson (d 1327; F 2) was first gm Kris
2 CONC tina Johansdotter (the family of the Elof Sons), who lived July 6 but died July 11, 1293, childless. About her see bd 13, and AF Liljeholm in PHT 1952. In his second marriage to Ingeborg Bengtsdotter (Folkungaättens teammate), Mr.
2 CONC  Birger had seven children (Gardell, 1, no. 159), four of whom apparently died early. The remaining were the Swedish National Council, the Lawman in Uppland, the knight Israel Birgersson (F 4) and the daughters Katarina Birgersdot
2 CONC ter and Birgitta Birgersdotter, the holy Birgitta (F 5), married to the brothers the knight Magnus Gudmarsson and the national council, the lawman in Närke, the knight Ulf Gudmarsson (Ulv ). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Finsta dynasty''',
2 CONT
2 CONT Finstaätten, a conventional family name on one of the Swedish older medieval noble high-relatives, formed after the farm Finsta in Skederid's sn, Seven hundred hd in Uppland. This farm was not an original pedigree of the family, b
2 CONC ut had been acquired by one of its most famous members the lawyer and knight Birger Petersson , the father of Saint Birgitta . Genealogy of the family in ASF 1. The original weapon of F is unknown. Knight Erland Israelsson, lawyer
2 CONC  Birger's uncle, brought a cross, his son knight Johan Ängel dy his grandfather's weapon, an angel, while lawman Birger took up his mother's weapon, two downward-facing wings. The prelates in F had varying seals without eating wea
2 CONC pons.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the testimony of Saint Birgitta's canonization process (Acta, p. 473), her father, lawyer Birger, is reported to have traveled to Santiago de Compostela and other sacred places and that her grandfather Peter Israelsson would ha
2 CONC ve visited Jerusalem, and that even older generations on the fathers would have piled on the said sites. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogically, one cannot go further back than to the layman's grandfather Israel, who was dead May 31, 1269, but who is otherwise unknown. A daughter of Israel was gm Anders And. Sons of them were the judge in Uppsala Andreas An
2 CONC dreae (And) and the lawyer in Tiundaland, the knight Israel Andersson (And). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons of the ancestor of Israel were the knight Peter Israelsson, Archbishop Jakob Israelsson (F 1) and the knight Erland Israelsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Israelsson is called dominee 1269 and was dead June 29, 1280; about his pilgrimage see above. He was GM a daughter of Birger Skänkare, who should have brought two wings in the gun (Rosman). Sons to them were the national tea
2 CONC m captain, the national council and the knight Birger Petersson and Israel Petersson, who became a canon in Uppsala in 1295 and in 1299 succeeded his cousin Andreas Andreæ (And) as domprost there. Mr. Israel was dead 24 Nov 1302. 
2 CONC His anniversary was celebrated in Uppsala Cathedral along with, among others, the cousin Karl Erlandsson's (see below) on Aug. 12, which was probably Israel's death day. Lagman Birger Petersson (d. 1327; F 2) was first gm Kristina
2 CONC  Johansdotter ( Elofssönernas ätt), who lived July 6, but was dead July 11, 1293, childless. About her see bd 13, and AF Liljeholm in PHT 1952. In her second marriage with Ingeborg Bengtsdotter (Folkungaättens lagmansgren), Mr. Bi
2 CONC rger had seven children (Gardell, 1, no 159), four of whom apparently died early. The remaining were the Riksrådet, the lawyer in Uppland, the knight Israel Birgersson (F 4) and the daughters Katarina Birgersdotter and Birgitta Bi
2 CONC rgersdotter , the holy Birgitta (F 5), married to the brothers knight Magnus Gudmarsson and the national council, the lawyer of Närke, knight Ulf Gudmarsson (the lawyer of Närke, knight Ulf Gudmarsson (Ulvåsaätten). ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Israel Birgersson, lagman Birger's son, had three children, of which Ramborg and Peter certainly, and Helena probably in Mr Israel's famous married. Of these, Ramborg Israelsdotter became 1) m Filip Nilsson (troll Sparre of Tofta)
2 CONC  and 2) m knight, the national council and the lawyer Anund Jonsson (Lion's face) as well as Helena Israelsdotter with the knight, the national council, the marsh and the lawyer Karl Ulfsson (Sparre of Tofta). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Israel Birgersson's son Peter Israelsson dy is little known. He was present as King Håkan's followers at Edsviken in 1371 and was not a knight. Peter's estate had been withdrawn by King Albrecht; Peter was last named as alive Nove
2 CONC mber 23, 1379 and buried in Vadstena Monastery March 24, 1384 (diarrhea). With him, Birger Petersson assumed the line.
2 CONT
2 CONT The father of Israel's third son, knight Erland Israelsson, is probably the dominus Erlendus, which is referred to as 1272 and 1276. He lived and is called Dominus 29 Dec 1279 but was dead 10 Dec 1288 and was buried in Sigtuna Mar
2 CONC iakyrka, where his burial ground is preserved (Gardell); it shows the weapon: a cross between two wings. Mr. Erland was gm Katarina Johansdotter, daughter of knight Johan Ängel dÄ. You know four children in Mr Erland's and Catheri
2 CONC ne's married. The daughter Ragnhild Erlandsdotter was probably the wife of Ragnhild, who before 2 October 1283 sold her fathers nursery Finsta to her cousin Birger Petersson (F 2). She was 1) with the knight Johan Karlsson (Fånöät
2 CONC ten), executed 1280, and 2) m the knight, the Riksrådet and the lawyer of Västmanland Magnus Gregersson (Folkungaätten's illegitimate branch). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Erland's sons were: the bishop of VästeråsIsrael Erlandsson (F 3), knight Johan Ängel dy and the canoe Karl Erlandsson. The knight Johan Angel (John Angelus) dy, mentioned dominee 1286, occupied his grandfather's name and arms.
2 CONC  Mr. Johan Ängel dy made his will on 12 Jan 1314 and chose camp town in St. Erik's chapel in Uppsala Cathedral and was dead on May 21, 1314. About his property etc. see ESF, 1, p. 38; he was married but childless. His brother Karl
2 CONC  Erlandsson (d. 1296) was 1286 canoe in Uppsala. Mr. Karl was a school in Paris in 1287 and studied at the University of Bologna in each case 1292-95. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Erland Israelsson's line began with Bishop Israel Erlandsson (F 3) in Västerås in 1328 or 1329, while the whole family began with Peter Israelsson dy about SEK 1384.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Finsta Dynasty, Band 16 (1964-1966), page 51, by  Bengt Hildebrand - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/Sbl/Mobil/Artikel/14142
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: 892==
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 12690531, Löing Contents: Hertig Magnus exchanges for Peter Israelsson (Finstaätten) soil in (Eds parish, Sollentuna hearad) to soil in Väsby (Munsö parish, Färentuna hearad).
2 CONT
2 CONT SDHK No: 935
2 CONT
2 CONT Dated 1274 February 13
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigtuna
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl (Tjälvesson) of Fånö announces that with his children's consent he has given shoe monastery his estate Salsta (Skoklosters parish), comprising 2 land lands, in exchange for its farm "Haraby" (formerly Hårby, Husby-Sjutolfts p
2 CONC arish), comprising 21 Öresland . In addition, the issuer of the monastery has received 6 trout land, of which each herb land is counted as equivalent to a land silver, and which are distributed as follows: 8 herb land in Lindberga
2 CONC  in Attundaland, 1 herb land in Gottrøre (Gottrøre parish), 10 money land in Tarv ( Close to the parish?), 2 herb land and 5 money land in Ovike (Husby-Långhundra parish), 4 1/2 herb land in “staui” and 1/2 island land in Haknäs (
2 CONC Vassunda sn, Ärlinghundra hd). The witnesses were the issuer's son John and daughter Ingeborg, Jakob Israelsson, Peter Israelsson, the steward "Ragni", the bailiff "Pauo" and others, and the sealants the issuer, Mr Gregorius, Mr J
2 CONC acob, Mr Peter and the issuer's sister Catherine.
2 CONT
