2 CONT
2 CONT Appears in the records from 1295, probably already a knight, probably 1296. Was councilor in 1297. Mentioned as Duke Erik's drots from 1302 and from 1307 also as Duke Valdemars. Between 17.5 1304 and 8.1 1307, he disappeared from 
2 CONC the Swedish diploma material due to exile and confiscation of goods. Died 1310. Owned Salsta in Lena sn in Norunda hd in Uppland and Ängsö in the same name sn in Yttertjurbo hd in Västmanland. Was married in 1296 to Ingeborg Ulfsd
2 CONC otter, daughter of the knight Ulf Karlsson (Ulv) and widow of the knight Knut Matsson, who was apparently a lawyer in Närke already in 1282, is mentioned as councilor in 1288 and died in 1289. Mrs. Ingeborg, who owned estates in K
2 CONC inds, Kåkinds, Vadsbo and Vartofta hd in Västergötland and in Karlstads and ölme hd in Värmland, died in 1307. In addition to the sons listed below, Mr. Abjörn had a daughter Ingeborg, who was certainly born in an illegitimate rel
2 CONC ationship, which Mr. Abjörn entered into before his marriage to his wife. Ingeborg. He gave this illegitimate daughter the same year he died, 1310, a significant gift with the consent of his mother and sister Kristina, all in acco
2 CONC rdance with what is stipulated in the Östgötland Act's Inheritance Code on gifts to free children. Had Ingeborg been born in a real bed, it is inconceivable that she or her husband, as the relationship was with the brothers' other
2 CONC  half-sister Birgitta, would not ever be found as a sponsor of the Abjörnssönerne's many business transactions. As a free child, however, Ingeborg did not belong to the family, even though she was recognized. She probably lived st
2 CONC ill in 1343, possibly still 1351. Was at least from 1310 married to Master Herman in Kavlebäck in Västra Ny sn in Aska hd in Östergötland, who lived still in 1320. Ingeborg owned estates in Åsunda hd in Uppland and in Aska, Dals a
2 CONC nd Göstrings hd in Östergötland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Abjörnsson, 1317, died 1359, knight, councilor, lawyer, drots. See tab. 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulf Abjörnsson, 1317, died 1347 el. 1348, knight, councilor, lawman. See tab. 4.
2 CONT __________________________________________
