1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Gustav Arvidsson (Sparre av Vik)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Arvid Gustavsson (Sparre av Vik) and Ramborg Israelsdotter (And) 
2 CONT * Born: after circa 1301 (only with another mother may he have been born before 1301).
2 CONT * Death: about 1366
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sparre_av_Vik '''Gustav Arvidsson (Sparre av Vik)'''] (son of Arvid Gustavsson). Appeared in the records from 1334. Became a knight at King Magnus coronation 21.7 1336. Mentioned as the nation
2 CONC al council from 1350, as a layman in Södermanland from 1355. Dog 1366 or 1367. His seat was probably Vik. '''Gave 22.8 1334 morning gift to his wife Kristina Petersdotter,''' who is mentioned as living 1329-1351, owned land in Ask
2 CONC ers hd in Närke and was the daughter of the knight and the Swedish National Council Peter Ragvaldsson (three squares) and Birgitta Jonsdotter (? Aspenäsätt ).  Mrs. Kristina was a widow of the Swedish National Council and Marshal 
2 CONC Erengisl Näskonungsson (split shield), who died on 29 March 1328, and whose son Erengisl Erengislason is also reported to be her.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children:==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ramborg Gustavsdotter,''' Buried in Västeråker's church in Hagunda hd in Uppland.
2 CONT * '''Birgitta Gustavsdotter,''' Buried in Västeråker church.
2 CONT * '''Daughter,''' however, no later than 1371 (RPB, no. 1009). Married to the Swedish National Council Finvid Finvidsson ( Frössviksätten ), who married Katarina Magnusdotter ( Aspenäsätt ) and lived for 1378.
2 CONT * '''Märta Gustavsdotter,''' Owned land in Västerrekarne hd in Södermanland and in Ydre hd in Östergötland. Died at the latest on March 21, 1384. Married to a knight by name unknown and married to the national council Folke Nilsso
2 CONC n ( Ivar Nilsson's family ), who married Ramborg Staffansdotter ( Ulv ) and died in 1400.
2 CONT * '''Arvid Gustavsson,''' 1356–1379, knight, national council, lawman. Appears at the earliest in 1356. Mentioned as national council from 1362 and as a layman in Finland from 1366. Became knight in 1372 or 1373. Appears as govern
2 CONC or of Lagunda hd in Uppland 1377-1388. Died in 1379 or 1380. Married at the latest in 1369 to Helena Magnusdotter, who probably lived still in 1373 but was dead in 1380, daughter of the knight and the national council Magnus Gisla
2 CONC son ( Sparre of Aspnäs ) and Birgitta Knutsdotter (family of the Algots sons ).
2 CONT
2 CONT == Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=s%c3%b6dermanland+lagman++&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=30&FacettState=undefined%3ac%7c&postid=sdhk_7402&tab=post#tab 7402]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1358 July 20, of Issue: Strangnas
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Matsson announces that he legally removed all his inheritance to his uncle Magnus Petersson after his uncle and the mentioned Magnus' brother Sigge Petersson, whether in "Sytho" or elsewhere, against as much land in Västergö
2 CONC tland, by agreement, as by their friends and kinsmen established between them. The shift has been legally made and fixed at the dog and team stings in Strängnäs Margaret Day 1358 in the presence of the '''knight Gustav Arvidsson,'
2 CONC '' a layman in Södermanland, and Mr Herman, church pastor in Taxinge. 12 fastes are listed.
2 CONT The issuer and Gustav Arvidsson and Johan Larsson seal. - https://lbiiif.riksarkivet.se/sdhk!7402_7402.jpg/full/1000,666/0/default.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Gustav+Arvidsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_4078&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 4078]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1334  augusti  22, of Issue: Vik
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustav Arvidsson giving his wife, Kristina Petersdotter in morning gift 4½ markland i Vik and just as much in Bonäs.
2 CONT Gustav Arvidsson, Knut, västgöta lagman, Nils Abjörnsson, Gisle Elinason, Stefan Röriksson, Anund Röriksson, Ulf Filipsson, Gustav Nilsson, Sigge Magnusson, Israel Birgersson, Håkan Magnusson, hans hustru Kristin, Johan Karlsson, 
2 CONC Fader Birgersson sealed. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/4078.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=6256 Spared by Vik, Related]
2 CONT '''Band 32 (2003-2006), page 798'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sparre av Vik, conventional contemporary after the weapon and the name of the farmhouse formed the name of a medieval high-salvation genus without contemporary genealogy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Its ancestor was Arnvid (Arvid) Gustafsson(d. 1317), which occurs earlier than 1301. He became a knight some of the years 1301–03. A has been identified with the Mr. Arvid who, according to the Erik Chronicle, as well as Abjörn Si
2 CONC xtensson, accompanied Duke Erik on his Christmas trip to the Norwegian King 1302. The identification is supported by the fact that he, like Abjörn Sixtensson (Sparre av Tofta) is mentioned among the dukes of Erik and Valdemar 1307
2 CONC . Of interest is in this context, also, that their families had the same weapons tincture, red saves in goldfields, that Abjörn Sixtensson's settlement with his mother in 1301 was sealed by A, and that A after Abjörn Sixtensson's 
2 CONC death was among those who took care of his children's interests. Thus, it seems likely that A and Abjörn Sixtensson belonged to the same family, but the degree of kinship should probably not be investigated. According to Erikkröni
2 CONC kan, A was killed at "Nyköping guest ban" by one of King Birger's men shooting an arrow through his chest. His seat is said to have been Ekholmen in Veckholm's snow in southwest Uppland, but his widow Ramborg, daughter of the lawm
2 CONC an in TiundalandIsrael Andersson (Duck , bd 1), lived at Vik in Balingsta sn, Uppland, according to his grave monument in Västeråker's church in the same landscape. At Vik, A and she had dated a letter in 1315. The 
2 CONT
2 CONT son Gustaf Arvidsson (Arnvidsson ; d. 1366 or 1367) appears from 1334 (DS 4, p. 390: the note), became knight at King Magnus' coronation on July 21, 1336, the council at the latest by 1350 and lawman in Södermanland some of the ye
2 CONC ars 1350-55. He belonged to King Magnus' son Eric's followers and later King Albrekts. In 1334, G had given the aforementioned Vik as a morning gift to his wife Cristina, daughter of the Council of State Peter Rangvaldsson (three 
2 CONC gin-beamed intersecting windows) and widow of Marshal Erengisle Näskonungsson (split shield; bd 14). Except in Uppland, he held land in Västmanland and Östergötland.
2 CONT
2 CONT G became the father-in-law of the Swedish National Council Finvid Finvidsson (Frössviksätten ; vol. 16, p. 643) and Folke Nilsson (Ivar Nilsson's family) and father of Arvid Gustafsson (d. 1379 or 1380). The latter appeared at the
2 CONC  earliest in 1359, and became the Council of Ministers by 1362. He was a lawman in Finland ("Österland") from one of the years 1364-66 to one of the years 1372-80, was dubbed knight in 1372 or 1373 and was governor of Lagunda hd i
2 CONC n Uppland 1377-78. As landowner, A can be invested in Uppland, Västmanland, Närke, Östergötland and Småland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A was the last on the mans side of his family but left behind his daughter Margareta Arvidsdotter (d 1415), who owned Vik 1382 and got married to the knight, the national council and the lawman of Uppland Ture Bengtsson (Bielke; b
2 CONC d 4). Their son Sten Turesson became the son-in-law of Karl Ulfsson (Sparre av Tofta, above), grandfather of Sten Sture dä and grandmother of Gustav I. Sten Turesson's daughter Katarina Stensdotter inherited Vik, who later was the
2 CONC  seat of her son Nils Olausson (S of Ellinge, p 783). 
2 CONT
