2 CONC nd Öresten to queen Margareta, participated in 1395 as a Swede in the peace negotiations in Lindholm and Helsingborg and 139Ö in the meeting in Nyköping and was in 1401 one of the leaders of Gotlandstäget. In 1415 he acquired land
2 CONC  in Östergötland against land in Södermanland. From Vadstena monastery he acquired the estate Herborum. In 1413 he was mentioned among the saviors in Gudhem County in Vestergötland. His wife's name was Cecilia and, according to Ra
2 CONC smus Ludvigsson, was the daughter of the Mecklenburg knight Gise van Helpten
