1 TITL Biskop
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Roe''' hadde vært kapellan hos biskop Matheus vest på Færøyene som døde i 1157, men først i 1162 ble Roe viet til biskop. Han var biskop frem til sin død ca. 1190. Hans datter, Astrid, skal ha vært mor til kong 
2 CONC Håkon Sverreson. Bror til Roe var Unas Kammaker. Han ble senere gift med Gunhild som hadde vært Sigurd Munds frille og som ble holdt for å være mor til kong Sverre. Sverre ble sendt til fostring hos Roe da han var 5 år gammel, dvs
2 CONC . ca. 1157. Der ble han opplært og viet til prest. Da Sverre ble født, etter sammenhengen i 1151, var hun gift med [https://www.geni.com/people/Unas-Kammaker/6000000000574567645 kammakeren Unas], som ble regnet for Sverres far. Ha
2 CONC n virket trolig i Bergen. Fem år gammel ble Sverre sendt til oppfostring hos '''Unas' bror, biskop Roe på Færøyene'''. Der fikk han geistlig opplæring og ble vigslet til prest, noe han etter eget utsagn egnet seg dårlig til. Da ha
2 CONC n var 24 år gammel, kom moren til Færøyene og fortalte ham hvem faren var. Da hadde hun vært i Roma, der paven gjennom hennes skriftefar hadde pålagt henne å fortelle sønnen om hans kongelige byrd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilde:
2 CONT * Biskopar ämbetstid: 1162–1174 Roe
2 CONT * Mogens Bugge: Våre forfedre, se nr. 787, 803, 804. Bent og Vidar Billing Hansen: Rosensverdslektens forfedre, side 52. 
2 CONT * Tekst: Tore Nygaard
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Links:'''
2 CONT * https://nbl.snl.no/Sverre_Sigurdsson
2 CONT * https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkjub%C3%B8ur_bisped%C3%B8mme
2 CONT * https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katolska_kyrkan_p%C3%A5_F%C3%A4r%C3%B6arna
2 CONT * https://books.google.fi/books?id=RrTCAgAAQBAJ&lpg=PT335&dq=Roe%2C%20bishop%20of%20the%20Faroe%20Islands&hl=fi&pg=PT135#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Google translate:
2 CONT Roe had been chaplain to Bishop Matheus in the west of the Faroe Islands who died in 1157, but only in 1162 was Roe consecrated a bishop. He was bishop until his death approx. 1190. His daughter, Astrid, is said to have been the m
2 CONC other of King Håkon Sverreson. Roe's brother was Unas Kammaker. He was later married to Gunhild who had been Sigurd Mund's concubine and who was held to be the mother of King Sverre. Sverre was sent to be fostered by Roe when he w
2 CONC as 5 years old, i.e. approx. 1157. There he was trained and ordained as a priest. When Sverre was born, after the connection in 1151, she was married to the comb maker Unas, who was considered Sverre's father. He probably worked i
2 CONC n Bergen. At the age of five, Sverre was sent to be brought up by Unas' brother, Bishop Roe in the Faroe Islands. There he received clerical training and was ordained as a priest, something he admittedly was not well suited to. Wh
2 CONC en he was 24 years old, his mother came to the Faroe Islands and told him who his father was. Then she had been in Rome, where the Pope, through her confessor, had ordered her to tell her son about his royal duties.
