2 CONT Canute I Eriksson (Old Norse: Knútr Eiríksson) or Knut Eriksson in modern Swedish (born before 1150 - died 1195/96) was king over all of Sweden from 1173 to 1195 (rival king since 1167). He was a son of king Eric the Saint and Kri
2 CONC stina (probably a granddaughter of Inge the Elder.
2 CONT
2 CONT After killing Charles Sverkerson in 1167, Canut, who had just returned home after ten years in exile, started fighting for power against Sverker the Elder's sons Kol and Boleslaw Sverkerson. Only in 1173 could he call himself king
2 CONC  of the whole country.
2 CONT
2 CONT Canute's able jarl from 1174 was Birger Brosa (died in 1202)
2 CONT
2 CONT Canute built a castle on the island of Stockholm in 1187, one of many such fortifications made necessary by heathen incursions from the Baltic lands.
