2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odon_of_Poznan
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Mieszko & his first wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1.         ODON ([1141/49]-20 Apr 1194).  The Chronicon Polono-Silesiacum names (in order) the sons of Mieszko III as "Ottonem, Stephanum, Boleslaum, Mesiconem et Vladislaum", specifying that (the first) two were born from "filia
2 CONC  regis Ungarorum"[272].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "duces Guenesie Odoiscius…Logeslaus" as sons of "Mesico"[273].  He succeeded in 1177 as ODON Prince of Posen and Kalisch.  m (after 1184) VIACHESLAVA Iaros
2 CONC lavna, daughter of IAROSLAV Vladimirkovich "Osmomysl" Prince of Galich & his first wife Olga Iurievna of Kiev (-after 1200).  The Chronicon Polono-Silesiacum refers to "dux Galatie" as the father-in-law of one of Mieszko's sons bu
2 CONC t does not specify which son (although he is named first in the list) or name the son's wife[274].  Baumgarten cites Polish sources which give her parentage[275].  Baumgarten cites another Polish source which names her and records
2 CONC  that she survived her husband[276].  Prince Odon & his wife had three children:  
2 CONT **a)         WŁADYSŁAW ([1190]-5 Jun 1239).  The Chronicon Polono-Silesiacum names "ducis Gneznensis Loczislai filii Odonis" when recording his daughter's marriage[277].  He succeeded in 1194 as Prince of Kalisch.  Prince of Pozna
2 CONC n 1227.  Prince of Greater Poland 1229.  -        see below.     
2 CONT **b)         ODON ([1191/92]-1225).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  The Annales Capituli Cracoviensis record in 1225 "Ordo de Kacich transfertur in Mogilan"[278].  Provost of Magdebur
2 CONC g.  
2 CONT **c)         RYKSA (-18 Nov after 1238).   Ryksa is shown in Europäische Stammtafeln[279] as the daughter of Odon but the primary source on which this is based has not been identified.  
2 CONT *2.         STEFAN . 
2 CONT *3.         WIERCHOSŁAWA LUDMILLA (before 1153-in Poland before 1211). ... m ([1167]) FERRY de Lorraine Sire de Bitsch, son of MATHIEU I Duke of Lorraine & his wife Berta [Judith] von Staufen (before 1152-7 Apr 1206). 
2 CONT *4.         ELŹBIETA ([1152]-2 Apr 1209, bur Kloster Dobrilugk).  ... m firstly ([1173/77]) SOBĚSLAV II Duke of Bohemia, son of SOBĚSLAV I UDALRICH Duke of the Bohemians & his wife Adelaida of Hungary (1128-29 Jan 1180).  m second
2 CONC ly KONRAD II von Landsberg Markgraf der Niederlausitz, son of DEDO V "der Feiste" Markgraf der Niederlausitz, Graf von Eilenburg [Wettin] & his wife Mathilde von Heinsberg heiress of Sommerschenburg (-6 May 1210).  
2 CONT *5.         JUDYTA (before 1154-after 12 Dec 1201).  ... m ([1173/77]) BERNHARD von Ballenstedt Graf von Aschersleben und Anhalt, son of ALBRECHT Markgraf von Brandenburg [Ballenstedt] & his wife Sophie von Winzenburg (1140-Bernbu
2 CONC rg 9 Feb 1212, bur Ballenstedt St Nikolai). Prince Mieszko & his second wife had five children: 
2 CONT *6.         BOLESŁAW (1159-13 Sep 1195). ... m ([1187/89]) --- von Pommern, daughter of BOGISLAW I Duke of Pomerania & his first wife Walburgis --- ([1162/72]-[1220/26] or after). Prince Bolesław & his wife had [three] children:
2 CONT **...
2 CONT *7.         MIESZKO ([1160/65]-2 Aug 1193).  ... Prince of Kalisch.
2 CONT *8.         WŁADYSŁAW ([1161/67]-3 Nov 1231).  ... m (before 1195) [LUCIA] von Rügen, daughter of JAROMIR [I] [Fürst von Rügen] & his wife --- (-19 Feb after 1208). ... 
2 CONT *9.         SALOMEA (-11 May <nowiki>----</nowiki>).  ... m (before 1177) RATIBOR von Pommern, son of BOGISLAW I Duke of Pomerania & his first wife Walburgis --- ([1160]-14/15 Jan 1183, bur Stolp).
2 CONT *10.      ANASTASIA (before 1164-after 31 May 1240).  ... m (26 Apr 1177) as his second wife, BOGISLAW I Duke of Pomerania, son of WARTISLAW I Duke of Pomerania & his wife --- ([1130]-18 Mar 1187). --------------------
