2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 OCT 1184
1 OCCU Bishop of Brandenburg and first ranked prince-archbishop of Bremen (1180-1184)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRANDENBURG,%20PRUSSIA.htm#AlbrechtMgfdied1170B
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         SIEGFRIED before 1138-[24 Oct/15 Nov] 1184, bur Bremen Cathedral).  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names (in order) "Ottonem, Bernardum ducem Saxonie, Sifridum episcopum Brandenburgensem, postea archiepiscopum Bremensem 
2 CONC et Hadewigem [uxor] Otto marchio Misenensis" as children of "Albertus Ursus"[96].  A 13th century genealogy names (in order) "Albertum, Berenhardum, Fridericum, Hermannum de Horlamund et Zeifridum Bremensem archiepiscopum" as the 
2 CONC five sons of "Albertus de Hanhalde marchio"[97].  Canon of the Franciscans at Magdeburg in 1164.  His election to the bishopric of Bremen, engineered by his father in 1168, was a direct challenge to the authority of Heinrich "der 
2 CONC Löwe" Duke of Saxony, but he was prevented from assuming the position by Duke Heinrich[98].  Bishop of Brandenburg 1173 until 1180.  Elected Archbishop of Bremen end 1179, installed in 1180.  
