2 CONT Emperor Friedrich II & his first wife had one child:
2 CONT *1.         HEINRICH (1211-near Martorano [12] Feb 1242, bur Cosenza cathedral). 
2 CONT **a)         HEINRICH (-[1242/45]).  ...
2 CONT **b)        ''' FRIEDRICH (-1251).'''  The Historia Sicula of Bartolomeo di Neocastro names "Henricus et Fridericus" as the two sons of "Henricus", son of "dominus Fridericus secundus…Romanorum…imperator", and his wife "dominam Al
2 CONC amanie", adding that they both died young "post decessum patris"[686].  The Chronica Senoniensis record that “Imperator Fridericus…filium suum Henricum” had two sons by his wife “filiam ducis Austriæ” but does not name them, addin
2 CONC g that “matri dicti Henrici” claimed that they were both later murdered by the emperor[687].  He was bequeathed the duchy of Austria and 10,000 uncias under his grandfather's testament, which specifies that he was the son of Heinr
2 CONC ich but does not name him[688].  He succeeded as duke of Styria, Swabia and Austria on the death of his paternal grandfather[689].  His death is recorded by Matthew Paris[690]. 
