1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sophia von Brandenburg=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Henry I, Markgraf von Brandenburg and Agnes / Anna von Wittelsbach 
2 CONT * '''Sophia von Brandenburg is Queen Elizabeth II's 14th great grandmother.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRANDENBURG,%20PRUSSIA.htm#JohannIdied12661267 Project MedLands, BRANDENBURG PRUSSIA]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''HEINRICH [I] von Brandenburg "ohne Land" (1260-14 Feb 1318).'''  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names (in order) "Albertum, Hermannum et Henricum" as sons of "Iohannes" and his second wife Jutta[336].  The Annales Lubicenses nam
2 CONC es "Agnetem filiam marchionis de Brandenborch, sororis Ottonis marchionis cum thelo et Hinrici marchionis dicti ane land"[337].  "Otto…Brandenburg et de Landesberg marchio" granted Schloß Querfurt to the bishop of Brandenburg, wit
2 CONC h the consent of "fratris nostri Hinrici…patruelium nostrorum Johannis et Wolmari, de Brandenburg et de Landesberg Marchionum", by charter dated 10 Jan 1305[338].  '''married  ([Nov 1298/19 May 1303], Papal dispensation Anagni 19 
2 CONC May 1303) as her second husband, AGNES von Bayern, widow of HEINRICH Landgraf von Hessen, daughter of LUDWIG II "der Strenge" Duke of Bavaria, Pfalzgraf bei Rhein & his third wife Mechtild von Habsburg ([1276/78]-22 Jul 1345).''' 
2 CONC  Her origin is confirmed by the charter dated 21 Aug 1323 under which "Ludowicus…Romanorum Rex" granted rights to "Sophie…sororis nostre Agnetis, relicte quondam Henrici Marchionis Brandenburgensis, filie"[339].  Burchard Archbish
2 CONC op of Magdeburg agreed an alliance with “Agn der Margreuinen von Brandenborch unde tu Landesberch”, with the consent of “hertoghen Hinrike von Brunswik erem swaghere”, by charter dated 16 Apr 1318[340].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Markgraf Heinrich & his wife AGNES von Bayern had four children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''JUTTA''' ([1299/1306]-[15 Jul 1325/early Feb 1327]).  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by the charter dated 16 Apr 1318 under which Burchard Archbishop of Magdeburg agreed an alliance with “Agn der Margreui
2 CONC nen von Brandenborch unde tu Landesberch” with the consent of “hertoghen Hinrike von Brunswik erem swaghere”[341].  '''married  (before 16 Apr 1318) as his first wife, HEINRICH von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen, son of HEINRICH I Herzo
2 CONC g von Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Grubenhagen und Salzderhelden & his wife Agnes von Meissen''' ([1289]-[10 Apr/8 Jun] 1351, bur Grubenhagen).  '''He succeeded his father in 1322 as HEINRICH II "der Junge" Herzog von Braunschweig
2 CONC -Grubenhagen.''' 
2 CONT * b)         * '''SOPHIE''' (1300-[1356]). "Ludowicus…Romanorum Rex" granted rights to "Sophie…sororis nostre Agnetis, relicte quondam Henrici Marchionis Brandenburgensis, filie" by charter dated 21 Aug 1323[342]. '''married MAGNU
2 CONC S I Herzog von Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Göttingen, son of ALBRECHT II "der Fette/der Feiste" Herzog von Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Göttingen und Braunschweig & his wife Richza von Werle ([1304]-[15 Jun/15 Aug] 1369, bur Lüne
2 CONC burg St Michaelis).''' 
2 CONT * c)         '''MARGARETE''' (1301-31 Mar 1347, bur Weissenfels St Klara).  Abbess of St Klara at Weissenfels.
2 CONT * d)         '''HEINRICH von Brandenburg'''  ([1302/10]-early Jul 1320, bur Prenzlau Marienkirche).  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRUNSWICK.htm#MagnusIGottingendied1369B Project MedLands, BRUNSWICK]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''MAGNUS von Braunschweig, son of ALBRECHT II "der Fette/der Feiste" Herzog von Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Göttingen und Braunschweig & his wife Richza von Werle''' ([1304]-[15 Jun/15 Aug] 1369, bur Lüneburg St Michaelis).  '''
2 CONC He succeeded his father in 1318 as MAGNUS I "der Fromme" joint Herzog von Braunschweig in Braunschweig und Göttingen, jointly with his two brothers.'''  “Otto dux in Bruneswich necnon Magnus et Ernestus fratres eius” donated prope
2 CONC rty to Hildesheim by charter dated 1 Jul 1321[338].  After the death of their older brother Otto, Magnus and his younger brother Ernst agreed on a partition of their territories, Magnus becoming Herzog von Braunschweig in Braunsch
2 CONC weig 1345.  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum records the death in 1368 of “Hertoghe Magnus vader de olde Hertoghe Magnus”[339].  Married:  '''SOPHIE von Brandenburg,''' daughter of HEINRICH I "Ohne Land" Markgraf von Br
2 CONC andenburg [Askanier] & his wife Agnes von Bayern (1300-[1356]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (1): GESA von Vechelde, daughter of ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus I & his wife had nine children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1).       '''''MATHILDE von Braunschweig''''' (-after 28 Jun 1354, bur Nienburg an der Saale).  m as his third wife, BERNHARD III Fürst von Anhalt in Bernburg, son of BERNARD II Fürst von Anhalt & his wife Helena von Rügen ([130
2 CONC 0]-20 Aug 1348, bur Nienburg Klosterkirche).).  
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2).         '''''MAGNUS von Braunschweig''''' ([1328]-killed in battle near Leveste 26 Jul 1373, bur Braunschweig Cathedral).  Co-regent of Braunschweig 1345.  Co-regent in Lüneburg 1367.  He succeeded in 1368 as MAGNUS II "Torq
2 CONC uatus/mit der Kette" Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg.  
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3).        ''''' ALBRECHT von Braunschweig''''' (-Verden 14 Apr 1395, bur Bremen Cathedral).  Provost of St Paul's 1357.  Kämmerer of Halberstadt cathedral 1358.  Canon at Magdeburg cathedral 1360.  Elected Archbishop of Bremen 
2 CONC 1360, installed 1363. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *4).         '''''HEINRICH von Braunschweig''''' (-after 26 Jan 1382).  Canon and provost of Heilige Kreuz at Hildesheim 1353/76.  Provost at Halberstadt cathedral 1367/82. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 5).         '''''OTTO von Braunschweig''''' (-killed in battle 16 Jan 1339, bur Nürnberg Franciscan church).    
2 CONT
2 CONT * 6).         '''''LUDWIG von Braunschweig-Lüneburg''''' (-5 Nov 1367, bur Wienhausen).  Co-regent of Lüneburg 1355.  m (contract 23 Jun 1355, dispensation Avignon 20 Jan 1359) as her first husband, MECHTILD von Braunschweig-Lüneb
2 CONC urg, daughter of WILHELM Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg & his second wife Maria --- ([1338/41]-after 16 May 1410).  The marriage contract between “Wilhelm Hertoghe to Brunsw unde to Luneborch...Mechtilde use dochter” and “Hertog
2 CONC he Magnus van Brunsw...Lodewich sin Sone” is dated 23 Jun 1355[340].  She married secondly (25 Jun 1368) Otto I Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg in Schaumburg und Pinneberg.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* a)         '''SOPHIE von Braunschweig''' (-13 Mar 1412).  Abbess of Möllenbeck 1386/1402.  Provostin at Gandersheim before 1402, Abbess of Gandersheim 1402.  
2 CONT
2 CONT * 7).         '''''ERNST von Braunschweig''''' (after 26 Feb 1385).  In Blankenau 1373.  
2 CONT
2 CONT * 8).         '''''SOPHIE von Braunschweig''''' (-1394).  m (before 24 Aug 1366) DIETRICH [V] Graf von Honstein, son of --- (-1379). 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 9).         '''''AGNES von Braunschweig''''' .  m (1360) HEINRICH Graf von Honstein in Klettenberg und Lohra, son of --- (-1408).   
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Magnus I had four illegitimate children by Mistress (1):'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT * 10).       '''''ALBRECHT''''' .  1367. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 11).       '''''HEINRICH''''' .  1367. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 12).       '''''MAGNUS''''' .  1367. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 13).       '''''OTTO''''' .  1367.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRUNSWICK.htm#MagnusIGottingendied1369B Source: Project MedLands Brunswick]
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sophie von Brandenburg'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia of Brandenburg-Stendal (1300–1356) was a daughter of Margrave Henry I (1256–1318) and his wife Agnes of Bavaria (1276–1345).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1327, she married Duke Magnus "the Pious" of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel (1304–1369), Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg. The following children reached adulthood:
2 CONT
2 CONT  d. circa 1356
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie von Brandenburg was the daughter of Heinrich I Markgraf von Brandenburg and Agnes von Bayern. She married Magnus I Herzog von Braunschweig, son of Albrecht II Herzog von Braunschweig-Göttingen and Rixa von Werle, circa 1327
2 CONC . She died circa 1356.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sophie von Brandenburg and Magnus I Herzog von Braunschweig
2 CONT
2 CONT *Sophie von Braunschweig+ d. c 1394
2 CONT
2 CONT *Matilde von Braunschweig+ d. a 28 Jun 1354
2 CONT
2 CONT *Ludwig Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg d. c 1367
2 CONT
2 CONT *Albrecht von Braunschweig d. 14 Apr 1395
2 CONT
2 CONT *Heinrich von Braunschweig d. a 1382
2 CONT
2 CONT *Ernst von Braunschweig d. a 16 Feb 1385
2 CONT
2 CONT *Otto von Braunschweig d. 16 Jan 1339
2 CONT
2 CONT *Magnus II Herzog von Braunschweig+ b. c 1328, d. 26 Jul 1373
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources:==
2 CONT
2 CONT *[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sophia_of_Brandenburg-Stendal Wikipedia]
