1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Canute V of Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT Not more than a year before his death, Canute married Helena of Sweden, but they had no children.[3] Canute fathered a number of children out of wedlock:[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Saint Niels of Aarhus (died 1180); he lived as monk[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Knud[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Valdemar; he was Bishop of Schleswig and Prince-Archbishop of Bremen
2 CONT
2 CONT Brigitte (or Jutta); she married Bernhard, Count of Anhalt
2 CONT
2 CONT Hildegard; she married Jaromar I, Prince of Rugia
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingerd; she married Casimir II, Duke of Pomerania
2 CONT
2 CONT Another daughter; she married Bogislaw III of Schlawe
