2 CONT ***C2. '''Boleslaw V "the Pious", Pr of Kalisch, Gnesen and of Great Poland (1243-79), *after 1221, +1279'''; m.1256 Jolante=Helene of Hungary (*1244 +after 1303)
2 CONT ****D1. Elzbieta, *1261/63, +28.9.1304; m.1273/77 Duke Heinrich V of Liegnitz (*ca 1248 +22.2.1296)
2 CONT ****D2. Jadwiga, *1266, +1339; m.ca 1279 King Wladislaw I Lokietek of Poland (*ca 1260 +2.3.1333)
2 CONT ****D3. Anna, a nun at St.Clara, Gnesen, *1278
2 CONT ***C3. Salomea, *before 1236, +1267/74; m.1249 Duke Conrad I of Glogau
2 CONT ***C4. Eufemia, +after 1281; m.1251 Duke Wladislaw of Oppeln (+1281/2)
2 CONT ** ...
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT =Boleslaw the Pious=
2 CONT
2 CONT Bolesław the Pious (Polish: Bolesław Pobożny) (1224/27 – 14 April 1279) was a Duke of Greater Poland during 1239–1247 (according to some historians during 1239–1241 sole Duke of Ujście), Duke of Kalisz during 1247–1249, Duke of Gn
2 CONC iezno during 1249–1250, Duke of Gniezno-Kalisz during 1253–1257, Duke of whole Greater Poland and Poznań during 1257–1273, in 1261 ruler over Ląd, regent of the Duchies of Masovia, Płock and Czersk during 1262–1264, ruler over Byd
2 CONC goszcz during 1268–1273, Duke of Inowrocław during 1271–1273, and Duke of Gniezno-Kalisz since 1273 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the second son of Władysław Odonic, Duke of Greater Poland by his wife Hedwig, who was probably daughter of Duke Mestwin I of Pomerania, or a member of the Premyslid dynasty. His name was very popular in the Piast dynasty, 
2 CONC so it's unknown exactly after whom he was named. Very soon Bolesław received the nickname of "the Pious" (Latin: Pius), given to him during his lifetime by the Chronicle of the Chapter of Poznań.
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1258 Bolesław married with Jolenta (Helena) (b. 1244 - d. 16/17 June aft. 1304), daughter of King Béla IV of Hungary. They had three daughters:[1][2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth (b. 1261/63 - d. September 1304), married in 1273 to Henry V, Duke of Legnica.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hedwig (b. 1270/75 - d. 10 December 1339), married in January 1293 to Władysław I the Elbow-high, Duke of Kuyavia and since 1320 King of Poland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna (b. 1276/78 - d. bef. 1300), a nun in Gniezno.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death without male heirs, all the Greater Poland Duchy passed to his only nephew Przemysł II. Crowned King of Poland in 1295 but murdered the next year, with his death the Greater Poland branch of the Piast dynasty becam
2 CONC e extinct.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source / Forrás:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boleslaw_the_Pious
2 CONT
2 CONT http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolesław_Pobożny
