2 CONT Izyaslav, Pr of Kursk (1125-29), Pr of Polotsk (1129-32), Pr of Turov (1132-34), Pr of Volynia (1135-42), Pr of Pereyaslav (1142-46), Great Pr of Kiev (1146-49)+(1150)+(1151-54), *Novgorod 1096, +Kiev 13.11.1154; 1m: apparently a 
2 CONC Staufen princess (+1151); 2m: 1154 N (Rusudan?) of Georgia; all children from 1m.:
2 CONT *A1. Mstislav II, Pr of Pereyaslav (1146-49)+(1151-55), Pr of Lutzk (1155-57), Pr of Volynya (1157-70), Great Pr of Kiev (V.1167-XII.1169)+(II.1170-IV.1170), +19.8.1170; m.1151/52 Agnieszka of Poland (*1137 +after 1181)
2 CONT **B1. Roman "the Great", Pr of Novgorod (1168-70), Pr of Volynia (1173-87)+(1188-1205), Pr of Galicia (1187-88)+(1199-1205), Grand Pr of Kiev (1203-05), *ca 1205, +murdered nr Zavikhvost 19.6.1205; 1m: bef 1184 (div 1198) Predisla
2 CONC va Ryurikovna of Smolensk (+after 1204); 2m: ca 1200 a Byzantine noblewoman (+after 1219)
2 CONT *** ...
2 CONT ***C3. Danylo, Pr of Galicia (1211-13)+(1229-64), Pr of Volynia (1215-64), crowned by a papal archbishop in Dorohychyn 1253/55 as 1st King of Galicia, *1201, +1264; 1m: 1218 Anna Mstislavna of Novgorod (+bef 1252); 2m: bef 1252 N,
2 CONC  niece of Duke Mindaugas of Lithuania; all kids by 1m.
2 CONT ****D1. Irakli, *ca 1223, +by 1240
2 CONT ****D2. '''Lev, Duke of Belz (1245-64), Duke of Halicz (1264-69), King of Galicia (1269-1301), he moved his capital from Galich/Halicz to the newly-founded city of Lvov/Lwow (Lemberg), *ca 1228, +ca 1301'''; m.1251/52 Konstancia o
2 CONC f Hungary (*ca 1237, +bef 1300)
2 CONT *****E1. Yuriy I, King of Galicia (1301-08), *24.4.1252, +24.4.1308; 1m: 1282 N Yaroslavna of Tver (+ca 1286); 2m: before 1300 Eufemia of Kujavia (+18.3.1308)
2 CONT ****** ...
2 CONT *****E2. Anastasia, +12.3.1335; m.before 1301 Pr Ziemowit of Poland (+1309/14)
2 CONT *****E3. Svyatoslava, a nun, +1302
2 CONT ****D3. Roman, Duke of Slonim and Novogrudok (1255-60), *ca 1230, +ca 1261; 1m: 27.6.1252 (div 1253) Gertrud of Austria (*ca 1288, +24.4.1299); 2m: ca 1255 Elena Glebovna of Volkovysk (+aft 1288)
2 CONT ***** ...
2 CONT ****D4. Mstislav, Duke of Lutsk (1265-89), Duke of Volynia (1289-aft 1300), +aft 1300; m.ca 1253 N, a dau.of khan Teigak of the Cumans
2 CONT ***** ...
2 CONT ****D5. Ioann Shvarn "the Lightning", Duke of Chelm (1264-69), Great Duke of Lithuania (1268-69), +1269, bur Chelm; m.1255 N, a dau.of Duke Mindaugas of Lithuania
2 CONT ****D6. Pereyaslava, +12.4.1283; m.ca 1248 Pr Ziemowit of Masovia (*1224, +23.6.1262)
2 CONT ****D7. Ustinia; m.1250/51 Pr Andrei II of Vladimir-Suzdal (+1264)
2 CONT ****D8. Sofia; m.1259 Gf Heinrich V von Schwarzburg-Blankenburg (+1287)
