1 NOTE Eleanor was an extraordinarily powerful woman, she was the duchess ofAquitaine and Queen of France (1137-1152) with her marriage to Louis VIIand Queen of England after her marriage to Henry. She was the Countess ofSaintonge, Angou
2 CONC mois, Limousin, Auvergne, Bordeaux, Agen. Eleanor had 10children, three of whom were crowned kings of England (Henry, Richard,and John). One of her daughters, Matilda, married Henry the Lion ofBavaria and Saxony and was the mother
2 CONC  of Otto of Brunswick; anotherdaughter Eleanor wed King Alfonso VIII of Castile and had Blanche, themother of Louis IX of France; her daughter Jeanne was the wife of KingWilliam II of Sicily and after his death, Count Raymond VIof
2 CONC  Toulouse."The Encyclopedia of the Middle Ages" Norman F. Cantor, General Editor.
