2 CONT Henry II (5 March 1133 - 6 July 1189), ruled as King of England (1154-1189), Count of Anjou, Count of Maine, Duke of Normandy, Duke of Aquitaine, Duke of Gascony, Count of Nantes, Lord of Ireland and, at various times, controlled 
2 CONC parts of Wales, Scotland and western France. Henry, the great-grandson of William the Conqueror, was the first of the House of Plantagenet to rule England. Henry was thefirst to use the title "King of England" (as opposed to "King
2 CONC  of the English").
2 CONT He is also known as Henry Curtmantle and Henry Fitz-Empress.
