2 CONT
2 CONT Henry the Lion had the following known children by his first wife, Clementia (divorced 1162), daughter of Conrad I, Duke of Zähringen and Clemence of Namur:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Gertrude of Bavaria (1155–1197), married first Frederick IV, Duke of Swabia, and then King Canute VI of Denmark
2 CONT *Richenza (c. 1157 – 1167)
2 CONT *'''Henry''', died young
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#HeinrichIRheindied1227A
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         '''HEINRICH''' (-Lüneburg 1 Nov ---, bur Lüneburg Klosterkirche).  The Chronicon Sancti Michaelis Luneburgensis refers to the son of "Heinricus dux" & his first wife as "puerum eiusdem vocabuli [=Heinricus]" specifying
2 CONC  that he was buried "ante altare sancta crucis"[457].  The necrology of Lüneburg records the death "1 Nov" of "Heinricus infans filius H ducis" and specifies that his father Duke Heinrich donated a mill to St Michael at Lüneburg i
2 CONC n his memory[458].  He died after falling from a table. 
2 CONT
2 CONT /!\ NOT his steepbrotther https://www.geni.com/people/Henry-V-Count-Palatine-of-the-Rhine/6000000001563248087 : 
2 CONT
2 CONT * e)   /!\      [https://www.geni.com/people/Henry-V-Count-Palatine-of-the-Rhine/6000000001563248087 HEINRICH] ([1173/74]-Braunschweig 28 Apr 1227, bur Braunschweig Cathedral).  The Chronicon Montis Serreni names (in order) "Heinr
2 CONC icum comitem Palatinum Reni, Othonem imperatorem, Willehelmus de Luneburch, Luderum" as children of "Heinricus dux de Bruneswich" & his wife "soror Rikardi regis Anglie"[477].  Heinrich accompanied his parents to England in 1182[4
2 CONC 78].  He campaigned with Heinrich VI King of Germany in Italy in 1190, but deserted in southern Italy and was outlawed at Worms in May 1192[479].  He was restored to favour by the emperor in Jan 1194 at Würzburg following his marr
2 CONC iage[480].  He succeeded in 1195 as HEINRICH I Pfalzgraf bei Rhein.  Vogt of Gotzlar 1204.  Deposed 1212.  Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg 1213.  -        PALATINATE. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
