2 CONT Count William was married twice. First, he was married in 1197 at Stavoren to Adelheid of Guelders, daughter of Otto I, Count of Guelders and Richarde of Bavaria. Adelheid died on 12 February 1208 while William was away on crusade
2 CONC . On his return he married secondly, in July 1220, Marie of Brabant, daughter of Henry I, Duke of Brabant and Maud of Boulogne and Alsace. She was the widow of Emperor Otto IV. William and his first wife Adelaide had the following
2 CONC  children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Floris IV, Count of Holland (24 June 1210 The Hague–19 July 1234, Corbie, France). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto (d. 1249), Regent of Holland in 1238-1239, Bishop of Utrecht. 
