2 CONT 8.         SOBĚSLAV UDALRICH ([1075]-14 Feb 1140).  ... He succeeded in 1125 as SOBĚSLAV I UDALRICH Duke of the Bohemians. ... m ([1123]) ADELAIDA of Hungary, daughter of ÁLMOS Prince of Hungary & his wife Predslava Sviatopolkovna
2 CONC  of Kiev ([1105/07]-15 Sep 1140). ... Duke Sobĕslav I Udalrich & his wife had five children:  
2 CONT *a)         VLADISLAV (-1165). ... m ([1152/55]) --- von Brandenburg, daughter of ALBRECHT I "dem Bären" Graf von Ballenstedt Markgraf von Brandenburg & his wife Sophie von Winzenburg. 
2 CONT *b)         '''SOBĚSLAV (1128-9 Jan 1180).'''  The Canonici Wissegradensis Continuatio Cosmæ records that "Lutherius rex" acted as godfather to "filium ducis Sobezlai" on Easter day 1128[192].  In prison 1147-1161.  He succeeded i
2 CONC n 1173 as '''SOBĚSLAV II Duke of Bohemia'''.  He was deposed in 1178.  The Cronica Principum Regni Boemiæ records the death in exile of "Sobieslaw II" after reigning for one year[193].  m ([1173/77]) as her first husband, ELŹBIETA
2 CONC  of Poland, daughter of MIESZKO III "Stary/the Old" Prince of Greater Poland & his first wife Erszebet of Hungary ([1152]-2 Apr 1209, bur Kloster Dobrilugk).  The Chronicon Polono-Silesiacum refers to, but does not name, the daugh
2 CONC ters of Mieszko III, naming (first in the list) "dux Boemorum Sobeslaus" as his son-in-law[194].  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Elizabeth filiam Meseconis ducis Polonie, viduam Zibizlai ducis Bohemie" as wife of "Conradus mar
2 CONC chio filius Dedonis"[195].  She married secondly Konrad II von Landsberg Markgraf der Niederlausitz [Wettin].  The Genealogica Wettinensis records the death in 1209 of "Elizabeth marchionissa"[196].  The Chronicon Montis Serreni n
2 CONC ames "Elizabeth marchionissa…soror Wlodizlai ducis" as wife of "Conradi marchionis" when recording her death "1209 IV Non Apr" and her burial "Doberluge"[197].  
2 CONT *c)         MARIA .  ... m firstly (29 Sep 1138) LEOPOLD IV Markgraf of Austria, son of LEOPOLD III "der Heilige" Markgraf of Austria & his second wife Agnes of Germany [Staufen] (-Niedraltaich 18 Oct 1141).  Duke of Bavaria 1139.
2 CONC   m secondly (after 1141) as his second wife, HERMANN III Markgraf von Baden and Verona, son of HERMANN II Markgraf von Baden & his wife Judith [von Dillingen] (-after 12 Jul 1153, bur Backnang Stiftskirche).  
2 CONT *d)         ULRICH (1134-18 Oct 1177).  ... He succeeded in 1165 as ULRICH Duke of the Bohemians.  Duke of Moravia 1176.  m firstly CECILIA von Thüringen, daughter of LUDWIG I Landgraf of Thuringia & his wife Hedwig von Gudensberg
2 CONC . ... m secondly as her first husband, SOPHIA von Meissen, daughter of OTTO "der Reicher" Markgraf von Meissen [Wettin] & his wife Hedwig von Brandenburg [Ballenstedt].  ... Duke Ulrich & his second wife had one child: 
2 CONT ** ...
2 CONT *e)         WENZEL (1137-in prison [1192]).  ... He succeeded in 1191 as WENZEL II Duke of Bohemia. ... 
