1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elisabeth von Hohnstein-Heringen=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Diederik III Count von Hohnstein-Heringen and Elisabeth von Waldeck.
2 CONT * During the Peasants' War , Hohnstein was still considered a safe fortress and was therefore visited by the abbot of Ilfeld Monastery to save himself and the monastery treasure. While the Counts of Hohnstein sealed the end of the
2 CONC ir rule at Lohra Castle (they died out in 1593), Hohnstein Castle came into the possession of the Counts of Stolberg through purchase in the 1st quarter of the 15th century , who took the complex militarily and structurally at gre
2 CONC at expense modernized (artillery tower) and expanded under [https://de.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burg_Hohnstein_(Harz) '''Count Heinrich zu Stolberg to a representative Renaissance castle.'''] During this time it became one of the larg
2 CONC est castles in the Harz Mountains.
2 CONT * [https://de.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stammliste_von_Hohnstein#Hohn1 '''Tribe list from Hohnstein'''] - B4. Elisabeth (* around 1312); ∞ I: (around 1330) Count Otto I. von Stolberg (* around 1310; † between November 24, 1337 and Janu
2 CONC ary 10, 1341), son of Count Heinrich V. von Stolberg (–1329/1347) and Jutta von Hadmersleben (-1347); ∞ II: (after 1337) Count Conrad IV of Wernigerode (* around 1310; † after June 24, 1373), son of Conrad III. von Wernigerode (12
2 CONC 97–1339) and Helena von Braunschweig-Lüneburg (-)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage I:''' Otto I, Graf zu Stolberg * c. 1305 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage II:'''' Conrad IV von Wernigerode 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children from Marriage I: Otto I, Graf zu Stolberg=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Heinrich XVI, Graf zu Stolberg * c. 1335  Elisabeth von Mansfeld
2 CONT * Sophie zu Stolberg
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children from Marriage II: Conrad IV von Wernigerode=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Conrad V, Graf von Wernigerode''' * c. 1350  Heilwig zur Lippe
2 CONT * '''Dietrich, Graf von Wernigerode'''
2 CONT * '''Albrecht, Graf von Wernigerode ,''' bispo de Halberstadt * 1346 + 1419
2 CONT * '''Heinrich IV, Graf von Wernigerode,'''  married Agnes von Gleichen-Tonna
2 CONT * '''Friedrich, Graf von Wernigerode'''
2 CONT * '''Sophie von Wernigerode,''' marrie  Otto von Hadmersleben
2 CONT * '''NN... von Wernigerode,''' married Friedrich von Heldrungen
2 CONT * '''Luckard von Wernigerode,'''  Married Ludwig von Roden und Wunstorf
2 CONT * '''Margarethe von Wernigerode'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://wikiscuba.com/wiki/Stammliste_von_Hohnstein '''Genealogical Register from Hohnstein''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * A4. '''Dietrich III. (V.) , Count von Honstein zu Klettenberg (1309), elder in the house (1306), built Heringen Castle together with his brother Heinrich (1327), founder of the Heldrungian line (extinct ...), documented from 128
2 CONC 6 to 1330, (* about 1279; † between 29 September 1329 and 4 May 1330); Von (between 1305 and 1310) Elisabeth von Waldeck († after October 24, 1371), daughter of Count Otto I von Waldeck (–1305) and Sophie von Hessen (–1331)'''
2 CONT * B1. '''Dietrich V.''' , co-chief of Honstein (1329), lord of Heringen and Tonna (1332), count of Heringen, Bockstedt and Honstein (1372), registered 1315 to 1372, (* about 1306; † 1379); ∞ I: (1326, before 22 February 1333) Adel
2 CONC heid von Holstein (* about 1299; † before 2 February 1350), (∞ I: (1313) Erich II Duke of Schleswig (* about 1288; † 12 March 1325 ), son of Waldemar IV Von Schleswig (1265–1312) and Elisabeth von Sachsen-Lauenburg (–1306)), daugh
2 CONC ter of Count Heinrich I (Holstein-Rendsburg) (1258–1304) and Heilwig von Bronckhorst (–1310); ∞ II: (about 1360, before August 24, 1366) Sophie von Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel (* about 1340, † about 1394), daughterDuke Magnus I (Bra
2 CONC unschweig-Wolfenbüttel) (1304-1369) and Sophie von Brandenburg (-1356))
2 CONT * C1. [I] '''Dietrich VI.''' , Greifi von Honstein zu Heringen (1378), first recorded documented mentioned 1373, (* about 1327, † after March 26, 1393); ∞ (before 4 May 1391) Lutrud von Mansfeld († 1394), daughter of Count Albrech
2 CONC t I von Mansfeld [4] (–1362) and Jutta von Schwarzburg-Blankenburg (–1358)
2 CONT >>>>>* D1. '''Dietrich VIII. Von Honstein-Heringen''' (1394), Leimbach , 1/2 Benneckenstein and 1/2 Hohenstein (–1417), documented in 1393, legalized 25 May 1417 in Göttingen , († before 27 January 1418 in prison)
2 CONT >>>>>* D2. '''Ulrich von Honstein, Canon of Halberstadt''' (1407–1422), (* 1384/1385; † after 1422)
2 CONT >>>>>* D3. '''Elisabeth von Honstein, in Heringen''' (1417–1439) (partim), documented mentioned 1416 to 1439, († between 16 April 1446 and 16 April 1447); ∞ I: Burchard (Busso) VII. Von Querfurt, first documented mentioned 1395 to
2 CONC  1404, († 1406), son of Gebhard XI. (IV.) Von Querfurt (1320-1383) and Mechtild von Schwarzburg-Blankenburg (1350-1370); ∞ II: (before 4 January 1418) Gottschalk von Plesse, first documented mentioned 1393 to 1435, († 1435/1437), 
2 CONC son of Johann von Plesse (1352–1360 / 1390) and Adelheid von Everstein (–1397)
2 CONT >>>>>* D4. '''Lutrud von Honstein-Heringen''' (1417–1432) (partim), documented document October 23, 1401 to April 24, 1446, (* about 1372; † April 24, 1446); ∞ (23 October 1401 in Rome, Eltville 24 January 1402 Dispens affinitatis
2 CONC ) Heinrich VII., Vogt og Lord of Gera, (* 3 May 1341; † between 26 February and 22 July 1420), (∞ I: (c. 4 December 1367) Elisabeth (Else) von Schwarzburg-Blankenburg, documented evidence from 4 December 1367 to 28 May 1399, (* c.
2 CONC  1341; † after 28 May 1399 before 23 October 1401), daughter of Count Heinrich XII. Von Schwarzburg-Blankenburg (1325–1373) and Agnes von Honstein (–1382/1389)), son of Heinrich V, sheriff and Mr. Gera, (1308–1377) and Mechtild vo
2 CONC n Käfernburg (1302–1375 / 1376)
2 CONT >>>* C2. [I] '''Heinrich VIII'''. , Recorded 1380 to 1392, (* about 1330; † before March 12, 1399)
2 CONT >>>* C3. [I] '''Irmgard''' (* um 1332; † 1366/1367); Rad Konrad von Tannrode, Herr zu Straussfurt, documented in 1356, (* about 1330; † between 17 July 1393 and 9 January 1394), son of Konrad (elders) von Tannrode (1297–1358) and 
2 CONC Sophie von Gera (1298- 1344)
2 CONT >>>* C4. [I] '''Elisabeth''' , registered in 1393, (* about 1334; † after 1393); ∞ (before 26 March 1393) Count Bruno V. von Querfurt [5] , lord of Vitzenburg (1372), mortgagor of Eckartsberga (1388), documented 1353, (* about 133
2 CONC 4; † between 25 November 1402 and 15 November. March 1403), son of Grave Gebhards XI. (IV.) Von Querfurt (1320–1383) og Elisabeth von Mansfeld [6] (–1358)
2 CONT >>>* C5. [II] '''Agnes''' , first recorded documented mentioned 1377 to 1394, (* about 1360; † 1 September 1404); ∞ (1377) Christian V Count of Oldenburg -Welsburg (* about 1342; † after 6 April 1399), son of Conrad I Count of Old
2 CONC enburg (1300–1368) and Ingeborg von Holstein -Plön (1316–1343)
2 CONT * B2. '''Heinrich''' , Canon and Provost Unser Lieben Frauen zu Halberstadt (1341–1358), Provost for the Holy Cross in Nordhausen (1349–1358), Cathedral Thesaurarius zu Halberstadt (1354–1358), documented 1315 to 1358, (* about 13
2 CONC 08; † between July 26, 1358 and June 23, 1360)
2 CONT * B3. '''Otto''' , first recorded in 1313, (* about 1310, † after 1315)
2 CONT '''* B4. Elisabeth (* um 1312); ∞ I: ( c. 1330) Count Otto I. von Stolberg (* c. 1310; † between 24 November 1337 and 10 January 1341), son of Count Heinrich V. von Stolberg (–1329/1347) and Jutta von Hadmersleben (- 1347); ∞ II: 
2 CONC (after 1337) Count Conrad IV of Wernigerode (* about 1310; † after 24 June 1373), son of Conrad III. von Wernigerode (1297–1339) and Helena von Braunschweig-Lüneburg (-)'''
2 CONT * B5. '''Bernhard''' , first documented mentioned 1315, (* about 1314, † after 1315)
2 CONT * B6. '''Ludwig''' , canon of Hildesheim (1360– before 1377), canon of Magdeburg (1360–1363), rector of Bibra (1360), canon (1360), rector of the Holy Cross in Nordhausen, archdeacon of Magdeburg (1361–1367), older cathedral zu Ha
2 CONC lberstadt (1369), first recorded documented mentioned 1360 to 1378, (* about 1317, † about 1378)
2 CONT * B7. '''Ulrich (Ulman) (III.)''' , Count von Honstein, Count of Kelbra (1372), Lord of Mohrungen and 1/2 Wippra (–1382), 1/2 office and Honstein Castle (–1412), mortgagor of Gelnhausen ( 1379), recorded from 1339 to 1412, (* abou
