1 NAME Otto der Schütz /Landgraf/
2 GIVN Otto der Schütz
2 SURN Landgraf
2 _MARNM von Hessen
1 NAME Otto II Landgraf von Hessen
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1322
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 DEC 1366
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otto_der_Schütz
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto II of Hesse, called Otto the Schütz (* before 1322; † December 1366 at Spangenberg Castle) was the only son of Landgrave Heinrich II of Hesse and his wife Elisabeth, daughter of Margrave Friedrich von Meissen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto married Elisabeth († 1382), daughter of Dietrich VII. von Kleve, in 1338. The marriage remained childless. From 1339/40 he was co-regent of his father and imperial governor in Mühlhausen. Otto participated, among other things
2 CONC , in two victorious feugs of his father (1356 and 1361) against the abbot Henry VII of Fulda. In 1356 he devastated the village of Hausen and the castle there, and in 1361 Otto and Margrave Frederick III of Meissen conquered and p
2 CONC lundered the Fuldian city of Hünfeld in 1361.
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto resided at Spangenberg Castle above the city of the same name, where he died in 1366. His unexpectedly sudden death gave rise to the assumption that he had fallen victim to a poison attack initiated by Abbot Henry VII of Fuld
2 CONC a. After Otto's death, Henry II appointed his nephew Hermann (1341–1413) as co-regent and heir in 1367.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The legend of Otto the Sagitter
2 CONT
2 CONT After one since the 16th. century, because his older brother Heinrich (who in truth did not exist) was destined to be an heir and he himself was destined to be a clergyman, left Otto and lived unrecognized as an archer at the coun
2 CONC t's court in Kleve. There he fell in love with the daughter Elisabeth (Elsbeth) of Count Dietrich. However, Otto's brother Heinrich died young, and since Otto was considered missing, Hesse threatened to fall to Duke Otto of Brunsw
2 CONC ick, who was married to a daughter of Henry II. Otto, however, was then recognized by a Hessian knight who was traveling through and greeted with great reverent, and Count Dietrich now agreed to a marriage of his daughter with Ott
2 CONC o. Otto returned with his bride to his father's court. 1]
2 CONT
2 CONT The material was often poetically and also musically processed, in dramas, operas, a novel, stories and lyrical-epic poems. The best known arrangement is that of Gottfried Kinkel, Otto der Schütz. A Rhenish story in twelve adventu
2 CONC res, from 1846.[ 2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In Kleve, Otto erected a large fountain stand, which first stood at the fish market, later at the end of the Prinzenhof. In the Old Auditorium of the University of Marburg there is a cycle of wall paintings "Otto der Schütz". The 
2 CONC Kinkel monument in Oberkassel, inaugurated in 1906, shows a scene from Kinkel's epic "Otto the Sagittarius" on one of its four relief panels.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HESSEN.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         HEINRICH (before 1302-Kassel 3 Jun 1376, bur Marburg Elisabethkirche).  Mitregent 1320.  He succeeded his father in 1328 as HEINRICH II "der Eiserne" Landgraf Herr von Hessen. … m ([3 Feb 1318/25 Sep 1320], divorced bef
2 CONC ore 1340) ELISABETH von Meissen, daughter of FRIEDRICH I "der Freidige" Markgraf von Meissen & his wife his second wife Elisabeth von Lobdeburg-Arnshaugk (Wartburg 1306-Eisenach 1367 before 10 Nov).  The Cronica Reinhardsbrunnensi
2 CONC s records the birth in 1306 of "Friderico marchioni filia Elizabeth in Wartperg" and her marriage to "Heinrico filio Ottonis lantgravii Hessie" in 1319[37].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich II & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         OTTO [II] "der Schütz" von Hessen (-[9/11] Dec 1366).  "Heinrich...Lantgrave zu Hessen und Otto sin Son", with the consent of “Grefen Gerlaches von Nassauwe unsers...Swagers, Grefen Johans sin Sons, u. Grefen Syfrides v
2 CONC on Widechinstein”, confirmed donateions to Mentze made by “Lantgrave Johan seligen...unser Vater Lantgrav Otte”, by charter dated 3 May 1347[38].  Mitregent as Herr von Hessen.  m (contract 25 Sep 1338) as her second husband, ELIS
2 CONC ABETH von Kleve, widow of GERAARD Heer van Voorne Burggraaf van Zeeland, daughter of DIETRICH VII Graf von Kleve & his first wife Margareta van Gelre (1307-Spangenberg 13 Nov 1382).  The marriage contract of "Dirk graaf van Kleef…
2 CONC zijner dochter Elisabeth" and "Otto zoon des landgraven van Hessen" is dated 25 Sep 1338[39].  "Didderic greue van Cleue, Aloph greue van der Marka, Margareta greuinne van der Marka onse…wijf ende Johan van Cleue doemdeken van Col
2 CONC en" issued a charter dated 16 Aug 1341 relating to the marriage of "Lysabet dochter ons greuen van Cleue" and "Otten audesten soen des lantgreuen van Hessen", recording "heren Gerarde heer van Voerne, dy haer man was"[40]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANCONIA%20(LOWER%20RHINE).htm#ElisabethKlevedied1382
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         ELISABETH (1307-Spangenberg 13 Nov 1382).  Willem III Count of Holland confirmed the financial arrangements for the marriage of “Heer Gherart Heere van Vorne en Burgrave van Zeelant” and “Veere Elisabette...dogter...Hee
2 CONC ren Dircx Grave van Cleve” by charter dated 11 Jun 1332[2204].  "Reynald greue van Ghelren ende van Sutphen" acknowledged that "Dyderic greue van Cleue onze…bole" had agreed to share "graescapen van Cleue" between "Margriete greui
2 CONC nne van der Marke, Elyzabeth vrouwe van Voerne, borchgreuinne van Zelant, ende Marie, sine dochteren" by charter dated 20 Aug 1333[2205].  The marriage contract of "Dirk graaf van Kleef…zijner dochter Elisabeth" and "Otto zoon des
2 CONC  landgraven van Hessen" is dated 25 Sep 1338[2206].  "Didderic greue van Cleue, Aloph greue van der Marka, Margareta greuinne van der Marka onse…wijf ende Johan van Cleue doemdeken van Colen" issued a charter dated 16 Aug 1341 rel
2 CONC ating to the marriage of "Lysabet dochter ons greuen van Cleue" and "Otten audesten soen des lantgreuen van Hessen", recording "heren Gerarde heer van Voerne, dy haer man was"[2207].  m firstly (before 11 Jun 1332) as his second w
2 CONC ife, GERAARD Heer van Voorne Burggraaf van Zeeland, son of ALBERT Heer van Voorne Burggraaf van Zeeland & his second wife Catherine de Durbuy (-20 Apr 1337).  m secondly (contract 25 Sep 1338) OTTO [II] "der Schütz" von Hessen, so
2 CONC n of HEINRICH II "der Eiserne" Landgraf Herr von Hessen & his wife Margareta von Meissen (-[9/11] Dec 1366). 
2 CONT
2 CONT No children.
