1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Erich I, Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Fürst Albrecht II von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen-Salzerhelden and Agnes von Braunschweig-Lüneburg
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.thepeerage.com/p738.htm#i7375 The Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Erich I Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen was born circa 1380. He was the son of Albrecht II Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen and Agnes I von Braunschweig. He married Elisabeth von Braunschweig-Göttingen, daughter of Otto II 
2 CONC Herzog von Braunschweig-Göttingen and Margareta von Jülich-Berg, circa July 1405. He died on 28 May 1427. He gained the title of Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of Erich I Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen and Elisabeth von Braunschweig-Göttingen'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Agnes von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen''' b. c 1406, d. b 13 Dec 1439
2 CONT * '''Sophie von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen''' b. c 1407, d. b 30 Apr 1485
2 CONT * '''Elisabeth von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen''' b. c 1409, d. c Oct 1452
2 CONT * '''Margaret von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen''' + b. c 1411, d. a 31 Oct 1456
2 CONT * '''Anne von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen''' + b. c 1414, d. 14 Oct 1474
2 CONT * '''Heinrich III Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen''' + b. c 1416, d. b 20 Dec 1464
2 CONT * '''Ernst von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen''' b. c 1418, d. c 1466
2 CONT * '''Albrecht III Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen''' + b. 1 Nov 1419, d. 15 Aug 1485
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_I,_Duke_of_Brunswick-Grubenhagen Eric I, Duke of Brunswick-Grubenhagen,by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Eric I, Duke of Brunswick-Grubenhagen nicknamed the winner (German: Erich I., Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen; c. 1383 – 28 May 1427), ruled the Principality of Grubenhagen, a part of the Duchy of Brunswick-Lüneburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eric was the only son of the Duke Albert I of Brunswick-Grubenhagen, who died in 1383, and his wife Agnes I, a daughter of Duke Magnus II of Brunswick-Lüneburg. Eric inherited Brunswick-Grubenhagen at a very early age; he stood un
2 CONC til 1401 under the guardianship of his uncle, Duke Frederick of Grubenhagen-Osterode. From 1402 they joined ruled the principality and Eric moved his residence to Salzderhelden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Disputes arose with his cousins Bernard I and Frederick I of Lüneburg, with the city of Brunswick, with his former guardian, with the counts of Schwarzburg and the Landgrave of Thuringia. All these disputes were soon settled again
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1406 Eric was captured in a feud with the Lords of Hardenberg in Lindau. He was only released after he gave them a written Urfehde and the city of Osterode am Harz as collateral.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1415, Eric declared war on the Counts of Hohenstein, because both sides claimed the county of Bad Lauterberg im Harz and defeated them near the village of Osterhagen. Count Guenther of Hohenstein died during the battle; Counts 
2 CONC Henry and Ernest were captured and had to pay 8000 florins and renounce their claims to redeem themselves.
2 CONT
2 CONT A dispute with the Lords of Bortfeld was settled soon after Eric entered into an alliance against them with the City of Brunswick. A dispute with Landgrave Frederick "the Peaceful" of Thuringia about the city of Einbeck was also s
2 CONC ettled quickly.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1422, the Abbess of Gandersheim Abbey (who happened to be his daughter, Agnes II of Brunswick-Grubenhagen) enfeoffed him with castle and city of Elbingerode. Two years, in 1424, the Abbess of Quedlinburg Abbey (Countess Adelhei
2 CONC d of Isenburg), enfeoffed the Dukes of Grubenhagen with Duderstadt, Gieboldehausen and the Golden Mark.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage and issue'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Eric was married to Elisabeth, a daughter of Duke Otto I, Duke of Brunswick-Göttingen (referred to as "Otto The Mad" or "Otto The Evil"). They had three sons and five daughters, including:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Agnes''' (1406–1439), Abbess of Gandersheim Abbey
2 CONT * '''Margaret''' (1411 – 31 October 1456) married Simon IV, Lord of Lippe in 1426
2 CONT * '''Anna''' (1414–1474) married first to Albert III, Duke of Bavaria and later to Frederick III, Duke of Brunswick-Göttingen-Calenberg
2 CONT * '''Henry III''' (1416–1464), who succeeded his father
2 CONT * '''Ernest II''' (1418–1466), who became provost of the St. Alexandri minster in Einbeck
2 CONT * '''Albert II''' (1419–1485), who succeeded his father
2 CONT * '''Elisabeth of Brunswick-Grubenhagen,''' who married Casimir V, Duke of Pomerania.
2 CONT
2 CONT
