1 NAME Henry the Peaceful, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1411
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lüneburg
3 STAE Braunschweig-Lüneburg
3 CTRY Deutschland(HRR)
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 DEC 1473
1 OCCU Herzog von Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p770.htm#i7697 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/D/per_page.php?id=1682 Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_the_Peaceful,_Duke_of_Brunswick-L%C3%BCneburg Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Duke of Brunswick and Lunenburg, Prince of Lunenburg''' joint reign with his elder half-brother [http://www.geni.com/people/Wilhelm-I-von-Braunschweig-L%C3%BCneburg/6000000003827363880 William the Victorious] Reign 1416–1428	
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Heinrich-I-F%C3%BCrst-von-Braunschweig-Wolfenb%C3%BCttel-und-L%C3%BCneburg/6000000003858624626 Henry the Mild] '''Successor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Bernhard-I-Herzog-von-Brau
2 CONC nschweig-L%C3%BCneburg/6000000003858815325 Bernard I]
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Duke of Brunswick and Lunenburg, Prince of Wolfenbüttel''' Until 1432 joint reign with his elder half-brother [http://www.geni.com/people/Wilhelm-I-von-Braunschweig-L%C3%BCneburg/6000000003827363880 William the Victorious] Rei
2 CONC gn 1428–1473
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Bernhard-I-Herzog-von-Braunschweig-L%C3%BCneburg/6000000003858815325 Bernard I] '''Successor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Wilhelm-I-von-Braunschweig-L%C3%BCneburg/6000000003827363
2 CONC 880 William the Victorious]
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was the son of Henry the Mild, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg. On their father's death in 1416, Henry and his brother William inherited the Principality of Lüneburg, while under the guardianship of the City Council of Lüneburg. 
2 CONC When the Duchy of Brunswick-Lüneburg was reorganized in 1428, Henry and his brother swapped Lüneburg for the Principality of Brunswick, including Calenberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Henry became of age, he tried to separate his and his brother's government. In 1432, he occupied Wolfenbüttel castle, and the brothers agreed to divide the territory: Henry received Brunswick and William received Calenberg, 
2 CONC Everstein, and Homburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry died without sons in 1473; his territory was inherited by his bother William.
