2 CONT
2 CONT Asdal
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Asdal, manor situated around. 6 km southeast of Hirtshals in Asdal Sogn, Vennebjerg Hundred, Hamilton County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical begins in 14. century, when the knight Niels Ovesen (Panter) and wife Joanna Andersdatter (Stenbrikke) owned it, then went in succession to their son væbneren Anders Nielsen (Panter) (- by 1406), 1393, wrote of the farm
2 CONC  and were married 2. time with Mrs Idea Lydersdatter (Holck). The latter writes in 1406 to Asdal and when she ægtede knight Sound Cable (the earliest-1440) to Fuglsang also wrote this in 1415 to it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Asdal Gods are on 553 hectares with Gammeljord and Saxtrupgård
2 CONT
2 CONT [Edit] Owners of Asdal:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1387) Niels Offesen Panter
2 CONT
2 CONT (1387-1393) Johanne Andersdatter Stenbrikke married Panter
2 CONT
2 CONT (1393-1405) Anders Nielsen Panter
2 CONT
2 CONT (1405-1415) Ida Lydersdatter Holck
2 CONT
2 CONT (1415) Sound Cable
2 CONT
2 CONT (1415-1422) Johanne Andersdatter Panter
2 CONT
2 CONT (1422-1450) Niels Eriksen Banner
2 CONT
2 CONT (1450-1479) Johanne Andersdatter Panter
2 CONT
