1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Sten Turesson (Bielke)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sten Turesson (Bielke), son of B. 6 , f. Probably around 1380, d. 1431 (buried in Vadstena Sept. 8). National Council by 1422 (on the other hand never became a knight); chieftain to Piksborg from 1426. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Married==
2 CONT
2 CONT Sten Turesson (son of Ture Bengtsson, to Örby and Vik in the Balingsta parish, both of whom belonged to his mother's family, Ekholmen in the Veckholm parish, which he obtained through his 1st marriage, both in Uppsala county, and 
2 CONC from 1419 Fogelvik in Tryserums parish, Kalmar county. Was resident at Ekholmen 1414. Riksråd latest 1422. Hövidsman at Piksborg 1426-02-02. Died 1431 before 27/6 and buried 1431-09-08 in Vadstena. He was later King Karl Knutsson'
2 CONC s guardian and foster father. '''Married (1st) in  1414 with Margareta Karlsdotter (Sparre av Tofta) ,''' in her 2nd marriage [married 1st: 1408 with the knight and chief at Turku Knut Tordsson Bonde, died in 1413 and in this marr
2 CONC ied mother of King Karl Knutsson], died about 1428, daughter of the knight, the Swedish Council and Marshal, the lawyer in Uppland Karl Ulfsson ( Sparre av Tofta ) to Tofta and Helena Israelsdotter ( Finstaätten ). '''Married (2) 
2 CONC o probably 1429 with Agneta Eriksdotter Krummedige,''' in her 1st marriage (married 2: o with Axel Nilsson to Barsebek), death (Bbl.) Between 1452-09-14 and 1453-06-01, daughter of the Danish national court master and the Swedish 
2 CONC Council of Representatives Erik Krummedige to Tranekärr and his 1st wife Beata von Thienen . She owned Örby, which she sold to her sister Johan Kristersson ( Vasa ) (Bbl.) In 1451 .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children with Margareta Karlsdotter (Sparre av Tofta)  ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Sten had two sons and three daughters, all born in marriage to Margareta Karlsdotter  (sparrow)
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Birgitta Stensdotter (Bielke);''' to Ekholmen after brother Knut Stensson's death 1451 (Bbl.) Lived 1461-01-02 but was dead (Bbl.) 1464-06-04. Married 1st before 1438-08-29 with the knight, the national council and the govern
2 CONC or of Kalmar castle Gustaf Anundsson Sture, dead 1444 (Pt XXI p. 103), and in this married mother of the governor Sten Sture d. o before 1446-12-02 with the knight, the national council and the lawman of Uppland Gustaf Karlsson (g
2 CONC um head) to Ekholmen, in his 2nd marriage [married 1st with Märta Karlsdotter. Married 3: o 1474 to Ingeborg Filipsdotter, daughter of Filip Axelsson (Tott)], Deceased 1486-07-26.
2 CONT * '''Ture Stensson, (Bielke);''' born about 1416. Arms. Council of Ministers 1436. Teamman in Uppland 1438-03-06 and also chief magistrate at Älvsborg in the beginning of the year 1439. Resumed a Norwegian attack on this fortress 
2 CONC in the summer of 1439. Then participated in the autumn of 1439 in the day of the reign in Telge (Bbl.), Where King Erik was finally deposed, and then accompanied his half-brother, Deputy Governor Karl Knutsson on his journey to Ka
2 CONC lmar, but fell ill just south of Nyköping and died after a few days, probably (1439) 23/10 and buried 1439-10-29 in Vadstena (Bbl .).
2 CONT * '''Katarina Stensdotter (Bielke);''' to Vik, lived widow 1458. Married 1438-10-00 with the Danish knight and the national council Klaus Nilsson ( Sparre av Ellinge ), to Ellinge in Skåne, lived 1449, but was dead 1452-02.
2 CONT * '''Knut Stensson (Bielke),''' to Ekholmen. Became a knight at King Kristoff's coronation 1441. Council of Ministers. Obtained at Karl Knutsson's ascension to Axvall Castle, but soon exchanged it for Nyköping Castle and County (B
2 CONC bl.). Lawman in Uppland 1450. Died 1451 and buried 1451-11-11 in Vadstena. Married [? 1: o with Kerstin Knutsdotter , daughter of Knut Bengtsson (Blå) to Arnäs. Married 2nd: with Elin Gustafsdotter in her 1st marriage [married 2nd
2 CONC  before 1455 with the knight and the governor Erik Axelsson (Tott), dead just before 1481-03-28]. Lived 1494-07-15 but was dead 1496-06-02, daughter of the knight and the national council Gustaf Algotsson ( Sture ) to Ängsö and La
2 CONC gmansö and his 2nd wife Märta Ullsdotter ( Sparre av Hjulsta and Ängsö ).
2 CONT * '''Margareta Stensdotter (Bielke),''' died 1439. Married at the latest by 1436 (Bbl.) With the Swedish National Council and the Governor of Stegeborg Nils Stensson ( Night and Day ), died 1439-10-00 in Norrköping (SK.). - https:
2 CONC //www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001330899240?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000140281852825
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children with Agneta Eriksdotter Krummedige==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Two sons and one daughter, dead young.
2 CONT
2 CONT == List of Swedish Diplomatarium's Medieval Letters from sok.riksarkivet.se
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Sten+Turesson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=8&postid=sdhk_20415&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 20415]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1425 January 26, Issue: Ekholm'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sten Turesson''' gives Harald Olofsson a letter of receipt on the accounts he has presented for the administration of Örby.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margareta Karlsdotter, wife of Sten Turason seals'''. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001330899240?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000140223356944
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Sten+Turesson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=12&postid=sdhk_19210&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 19210]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1419 January 25, of Issue: Uppsala'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The gunman '''Sten Turesson agrees with his wife Margareta Karlsdotter's''' consent and with certain conditions to two prebendas in Uppsala Cathedral land in the following farms, namely in Vallby, "Endista" and Fantebo in Viksta s
2 CONC n, Norunda hd, in "Alsekeby" and Kibrunna in Ramsta sn , in Norsta, "Bærby" and "Bersta" in Balingsta sn and in Brunna (?), as well as a mill in Tensta sn, Norunda hd. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/19210.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Sten+Turesson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=15&postid=sdhk_20589&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 20589]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT *'''Dating: 1425 October 25
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sten Turesson (Bielke) sells, with his wife Margareta Karlsdotter (Sparre av Tofta)''' and her stepson Karl Knutsson (Bonde) as co-sigilants, to Kristiern Nilsson (Vaasa) land in Håbo and Sollentuna herds in Uppland, Snevringe 
2 CONC herad in Västmanland, and Väster - and the Austrians are hardening in Södermanland, for a total of DKK 2318. SDHK No: 25494, Archbishop Jöns i Uppsala, Margareta Eriksdotter, widow of Kristiern Nilsson, Erik Nipertz, Erik Turesson
2 CONC  and Kristiern Bengtsson , knight, attest that they and other Messrs. Kristiern's heirs collected stated sums for goods, which King Karl repurchased by Mr Kristiern, and as Kristiern Nilsson acquired on various occasions by Mr. St
2 CONC en Turesson, Mrs. Margareta (King Charles's mother) and Karl Bonde, namely: 3 land land in Tofta on Alsnö and more for 400 English nobles (SDHK no. 20986 ); 3 farms in Rumby in Ed's parish and more for FIM 2,318 (SDHK no. 20589 );
2 CONC  3 farms in Hummelsta and more for 50 English nobles (SDHK no. 21545 ); land in Sparrsätra church village and more for 220 English nobles (SDHK no. 21009); land in Lundersta in Fittja parish and more for 150 English nobles (SDHK n
2 CONC o. 21410 ); farms in Limsta and more in Irsta parish for 200 Swedish marks (letter missing; SDHK no. 44741 ) and in Sylta in the same parish for 28 barrels of iron (SDHK no. 20604 ); a farm in Västerås for 2 1/2 read iron (letter 
2 CONC missing; SDHK no 44742 ) - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000001330899240&photo_id=6000000140281852825&position=0
2 CONT
