2 _MARNM Turesdotter (Bielke)
2 NICK Märta
1 SEX F
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1379
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Margareta/Märta Turesdotter==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Ture Kettilsson (Bielke) and Sigrid Nilsdotter (Natt och Dag) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=M%c3%a4rta+turesdotter+vadstena&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_10989&tab=post#tab 10989]
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 13770330, Vadstena Monastery
2 CONT Contents: Bishop Valdemar (Podebusk) in Odense announces that, in accordance with the assignment given to him by Pope Gregory XI, he arrived in Vadstena monastery to conduct a full investigation of the deceased wife Birgitta, tran
2 CONC sferred from Rome to Vadstena, her life and morals and even the miracles that have happened through her merits. In Vadstena, high-ranking gentlemen and wives from all over the kingdom of Sweden were gathered, who have been with Bi
2 CONC rgitta ever since the youth. These persons testified in the presence of Bishop Nils (Hermansson) in Linköping, Nils Johansson (Feet), dean in Uppsala and canoe in Linköping, Lars Ödesson, canoe (in Linköping), Henrik Hennekesson, 
2 CONC prebendate at Linköping Cathedral, and the knight Vicke van Vitzen, chief white man at Kalmar castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT First, the knight [https://www.geni.com/people/Karl-Magnusson-%C3%96rnfot/6000000005080868879 Karl Magnussons] testified to his wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Margareta-Turesdotter-Bielke/ 6000000003897416129 Märta (Turesdotter
2 CONC  Bielke)] by Broby, '' 'who was 60 and widowed for 33 years' ''. She had known Birgitta since her youth and testified that Birgitta always served God and devoted herself to prayers, alms, and other works of devotion. After Birgitt
2 CONC a's marriage, she had a special house for the poor and the sick; every day she visited the sick and distributed supplies to them and also appointed others to the same task. She had a daily habit of always attending the service bef
2 CONC ore the noon meal, and then she worked on the decoration of the altar and priestly costumes and more. In the absence of her husband, she was lying on a hard and uncomfortable bed at night and during the day she was dressed in heav
2 CONC y clothing. Witnesses present at Mrs Märta's testimony were Nils Johansson (Feet), dean of Uppsala and canoe in Linköping, as well as Tord Andersson and Ragvald Anundsson, canoe in Linköping.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingeborg, daughter of the knight Bo (Nilsson), was 60 years old and had lived as a widow for 27 years. She testified, in the presence of the same witnesses as above, that Birgitta, during her youth, led a virgin life and disregard
2 CONC ed all effervescence and unclean acts. Since marrying, she devoted herself to prayer, worship, and fasting and gifts to the poor. After her husband's death, she lived as a widow for 33 years. The knight Erik (Turesson's) daughter 
2 CONC Ingeborg, who was 50 years old and had lived as a widow for 13 years, stated that she got to know Birgitta after she got married. Ingeborg testified, among other things, that Birgitta lived simply and without ornaments of gold or 
2 CONC silver. She chastised her body by wearing hard and hard clothes, both in bed at night and in the day, and she tried to persuade her husband to live as she did. Both before and after her husband's death, Birgitta gathered poor peop
2 CONC le and listened in a special house, and together with other selected persons she gave them all the necessities and had the baths prepared and washed their bodies. Further, she taught her husband, who was an uneducated layman, amon
2 CONC g other things, to read the Holy Virgin's prayers. After becoming a widow, she immediately removed all bodily ornaments in Sweden and put on a tough and simple garment of sheepskin; she also avoided all the luxury of her food. Thr
2 CONC ough her words, she led women in different places with poor living to a good life and remedy. Ingeborg stayed with Birgitta for five years, when she also visited the saints' tombs with her so often that the forces ceased. Birgitta
2 CONC  longed for Christ to such an extent that she did not want to hear about the vain splendor of the world, which was once in Rome, or to turn her eyes to it. She was constantly praying with tears in churches or in private places, an
2 CONC d every day she sang the prayers with her own voice along with the priests who prayed with her, before going around to the tombs of the saints to proclaim. Furthermore, she confessed daily and abstained from all weakening.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Magnus Gudmarsson's daughter Ingeborg, wife of Earl Erengisle (Sunesson), was 50 years old and testified, with the above witnesses present, that Birgitta always devoted herself to prayer both in the morning and in the afternoo
2 CONC n, and in her spare time she served the poor. The knight Nils Dannes daughter Iliana, wife of Nils Håkansson (Läma), was 48, spent time with Birgitta during her marriage and testified that Birgitta let poor, sick and listen to her
2 CONC  farm where she gave them shelter in a large building which was intended for this purpose. As a servant she gave them honorable wives who gave them food and all the necessities. Every day, Birgitta washed her feet on twelve of the
2 CONC  poor, especially on Fridays but also on other days. She lived a hard life day and night when her husband was absent. When he passed away, she left the splendor of this world and lived in the Alvastra monastery of the Order of the
2 CONC  Cistercian, where Birgitta buried her husband and served God in coarse clothing until she went to Rome. Every day she confessed, both while living in her house and in the monastery. If she uttered a harsh word
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Karl+Magnusson++vadstena&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=7&postid=sdhk_11209&tab=post#tab 11209]
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 13780409, Vadstena Contents: Märta Turesdotter in Broby surrenders for his and his parents' sea bag 5 ounces of land in the village of Harsby in Å parish on the Vikbolandet to Vadstena monastery, which land accrued to her 
2 CONC through inheritance after the death of her parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer seals together with his son Erik Karlsson, his grandsons Karl Magnusson and Karl Bengtsson, Bishop Nils (Hermansson) in Linköping and Earl Erengisle (Sunesson).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Medieval transcriptions:  [A] in hs C 46, fol. 129v-132v, UUB; [B] i hs A 14, fol. 24r-28r, Kungl. the library, Stockholm; [C] in Liber privilegiorum monasterii Vadstenensis, hs A 19, fol. 41v-42r, RA (preamble only, see textnot
2 CONC  al-al); [D] in Cod. Harl. 612, vol. 215r-216v, British Library, London; [E] Cod. Ottob. lazy. 90, vol. 22v-25r, Vatican Library. - The pretzels also. in C 46 (UUB) fol. 128R; C 172 (UUB) fol. 47v
2 CONT * Medieval regest / note:  in notarial instrument. by Lambertus Hermanni. In the vidim. 1377 1/4, Vadstena (SDHK no. 10990 ).
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcriptions:  Örnhielm: Bull. In pp. 1341-1342
2 CONT * SRS III: 2, pp. 220-223, 231-232 (excerpt after B) I. Collijn, ed., Acta et processus canonizacionis beate Birgitte (1924-1931), pp. 62-71 (after B) Dipl. Dan. IV: 1, No. 216 (excerpted after C and D).
2 CONT * A 19: Corpus Codicum Suecicorum XI (1950); A 14: Manuscripts from the Middle Ages of Sweden I
2 CONT * For the testimonies, see T. Höjer, Studies in the History of the Vadstena Monastery and the Order of the Birgit order until the mid-14th century (1905), pp. 103-104 with note 4; T. Nyberg, Birgitine Party Gift (1991), p. 411; A.
2 CONC  Fröjmark, Miracles and Saint Cult (1992), p. 41.
2 CONT * For the miracle see J. Myrdal-G. Bäärnhielm, Women, Children and Parties in Medieval Miracle Stories (1994), pp. 24, 139.
2 CONT * About Bo Nilsson (Natt og Dag) and his daughter Ingeborg, who through his marriage to Johan Tomasson was the mother of the boyfriend Bo Jonsson, see Elgenstierna V: Natt och Dag, pp. 386-387.
2 CONT * About the knight Karl Magnusson (Örnfot) and his wife Märta Turesdotter (Bielke), see ÄSF I, p. 311 f.
2 CONT * About the knight Magnus Gudmarsson (Ulvåsaätten) and his daughter Ingeborg, see ÄSF I; p. 92.
2 CONT * Kristina Bosdotter is likely to be identified as the wife of Johan Götesson, County Governor of Göstrings County; see Letters 1366 8/12 (DS No. 7301) and 1368 19/3 (DS No. 7677).
2 CONT * About Elin Lydersdotter see letter 1375 26/3 (DS no. 8750).
2 CONT * The monk Lars in Alvastra is probably identical with a person of this name mentioned in letter 1385 9/3 (SDHK no. 12823 ). About Daniel, mentioned as abbot in Alvastra in letter 1358 7/2 (DS no. 5851), see E. Ortved, The Order o
2 CONC f the Cistercian and its Monasteries in the Nordic Region 2 (1933), pp. 104-105.
