3 CTRY Sweden
1 OCCU Väpnare i Länghem, Väpnare
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Peder Pedderson, till Hagalsrum, (Nr. 59)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Peder Hakansson, till Hagelsrum and Carin Gustafsdotter 
2 CONT *  Father PEDER HÅKANSSON, gunner, is mentioned, among other things, in an act, dat. Länghen (in Kinds herald) 11/8 1488 and his brother-in-law Arvid Knutsson to Torpa and others. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000006128072452&photo_id=6000000118104098821&position=0 '''Christina Hakansdotter, af Wangaslagten,'''] daugter of Hovidsmannen pa Westeras Haken Svensson 
2 CONC (Bolja eller Stromfelt) and Anna Karlsdotter (Bonde), daughter of King Charles VIII of Sweden & Kristina Abrahamsdotter 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Håkan Pedersson,''' Håkan Persson, died about 1531, married 1st before 1514 with Kerstin Håkansdotter (Tun) , daughter of the gunner Håkan Karlsson Tun and Ingrid Knutsdotter ( spar over star ).  Håkan Pedersson to Flagelsrnm
2 CONC  and Dansjö and Attorp and Tranetorp in Westergöt Bland; Was 1530 and 1550 Stath8llare in Westergöthland and brought a white hand in blue field. - Married to Christina Thun;  daughter of Hakan Fadersson Thun, of Attorp and Ericsst
2 CONC ada, who brought in the weapon a growing crescent with face and two stars facing each other, and Ingegerd Knutsdotter (Drake af Intorp or Store). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' [http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Hand_nr_59 Adelsvapen Hand nr #59]
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT Known member was Field Colonel, Knut Håkansson Hand to Attorp and Hagelsrum, who in 1554 became commander of Östbo, Västbo and Sunnerbo and in 1564-65 held several important commands in the war against Denmark. He led a ravage tra
2 CONC in to Halland in January 1564, fought in July against Daniel Rantzau in Småland and in September became field commander in Blekinge. In 1565 Hand first served as "field marshal" (equestrian commander) in Småland and in the summer,
2 CONC  as field colonel, made an incident in Halland, where he (August 16) burned Falkenberg. After the other Swedish army came down, Hand participated in the conquest of Varberg (September 15) and led a division of footmen in the unfor
2 CONC tunate battle of the Swedes at Axtorna, where he fell during the retreat (October 20, 1565). - One of his sons, Arvid Knutsson, took the mother's name Drake and became the ancestor of the noble family Drake af Hagelsrum, another, 
2 CONC Håkan Hand, in 1633 as governor of Kronoberg county and governor of Kronoberg castle, was married to Erik XIV's  daughter Virginia. His son Erik Hand, introduced at the knight's house in 1625, died as Lieutenant Colonel in 1632 in
2 CONC  Ingolstadt from the wounds he received during the storming attempt against Alte Veste near Nuremberg. This branch of food was sealed on the sword side by his younger brother, County Chief Johan Hand. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Squire. Mentioned among others. a. in an act, dat. Länghem (in Kinds hearth) 1488-08-11 along with his brother-in-law Arvid Knutsson to Torpa with fl.  Married to Karin Gustafsdotter, daughter of the knight and the national counci
2 CONC l Gustaf Olofsson to Tofta and Erikstad, of the older Capricorn family, and his 1st wife Ingrid Bengtsdotter (Vinstorpsätt). (The Knight's Pedigree-Hand) The first time the hand as a shield mark is legally appearing in a preserved
2 CONC  medieval document is in a parchment letter dated May 1, 1400, in which an Atte Pedarson as a witness with his name and weapon, one hand confirms a mortgage deed of a farm in Köping. His kinship with the introduced family is certa
2 CONC inly not proven, although his first name, compiled with the name of the family Hand's oldest tribal Attorp, or according to the original name form Attetorp, could possibly give rise to suspicion of a relationship. Nor is there any
2 CONC  demonstrable relationship between this family and the "my and the lovely troman" Nils Pedersson, who on March 17, 1508 in Vadstena by the governor of Svante Nilsson Sture obtained freedom and salvation on his goods and farms and 
2 CONC to arms a white hand in red field. This Nils Pedersson is recorded on the Knights House board as brother of Håkan Pedersson, although such a relationship is completely unknown to older genealogists. The weapons are also significan
2 CONC tly different, in that Nils Pederssons shows a left hand - with the thumb to the right - while the hand in Håkan Pedersson's weapon is a right hand in blue field. (Both weapons have the flatside of the hand facing forward, which i
2 CONC s the image in the arms books of the Hand-eagle's weapons with a backward hand is incorrect.) The family had its original residence in Kinds herd, where it enjoyed old salvation and was closely associated with its noble family of 
2 CONC saviors. in it Nils Pederssons shows a left hand - with the thumb to the right - while the hand in Håkan Pedersson's weapon is a right hand in blue field. (Both weapons have the flatside of the hand facing forward, which is the im
2 CONC age in the arms books of the Hand-eagle's weapons with a backward hand is incorrect.) The family had its original residence in Kinds herd, where it enjoyed old salvation and was closely associated with its noble family of saviors.
2 CONC  in it Nils Pederssons shows a left hand - with the thumb to the right - while the hand in Håkan Pedersson's weapon is a right hand in blue field. (Both weapons have the flatside of the hand facing forward, which is the image in t
2 CONC he arms books of the Hand-eagle's weapons with a backward hand is incorrect.) The family had its original residence in Kinds herd, where it enjoyed old salvation and was closely associated with its noble family of saviors.
2 CONT
