2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Daughter of  Birger Birger Jarl MAGNUSSON FOLKUNGE (~1200 - 1266) & Ingeborg ERIKSDOTTER (1214 - 1254)''' 
2 CONT * [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#BirgerMagnussondied1266B '''KRISTINA Birgersdotter''' (-after 1285).  Married SIGGE Guttormsson, from Ljuna (-bur Alvastra Abbey).]
2 CONT * [http://samla.raa.se/xmlui/bitstream/handle/raa/1098/1935_237.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y '''Death Record:''' 1273-02-05 Östergötland, Näsby i Åkerbo hd]
2 CONT * Kristina Birgersdotter is mentioned several times as married to the knight Sigge Guttormsson (two lilies with stems, rising from an open rose).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000009365755840?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000116462334837 '''Sigge Guttormsson of Ljuna,'''] GUTTORMSSON (TVÅ LILJESTAVAR SNETT NEDSKJUTANDE FRÅN SÄNKT ROS). and mother-in
2 CONC -law to the lords Lidinvard Ödesson (Örnfot) and to the national council Ulf Holmgersson (Ama). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Birger Siggesson (gumsehuvud),''' Oh my dear, my dear, I give my furded coat with a capuchon - for my son Birger, this armor as a whole, as I have had." The young son Birger gets his father's armor, because he seems to be ded
2 CONC icated to a worldly career as a knight. 
2 CONT * '''Helena Siggedotter;''' Their daughter Helena's daughter has to have been married first to the Danish knight Ingemar Nielsen, and Then to Ulf Holmgersson (Ama). A son is also known by Siggy Guttormssons Testament, written 11 J
2 CONC une 1283
2 CONT * '''Margaret Siggesdotter'''
