1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Märta Knutsdotter (Tre rosor), till Mörby=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Knut Jönsson (Tre rosor) and Kristina Bengtsdotter (Hafridssons ätt)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Tre_rosor Tre rosor, by Adelsvapen]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TAB 1'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut (known only through his children's patronymics). Married to Christina in Haneström in Fuxerna parish who died in 1346 at the earliest, daughter of the Riksdag and lawman Bengt Hafridsson .
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Folke Knutsson'''. Domprost in a crowd.
2 CONT * '''Jon Knutsson,''' Married 1st before 1360 to a daughter of Nils Tyrgilsson (Färla) and Ingeborg Eskilsdotter (Lejonlilja). Married to Märta Jönsdotter (who remarried before 1386 to Björn Elefsson), daughter of the knight and c
2 CONC ouncilor Jöns Hiärne and Christina Nilsdotter (Rane Jonsson's family).
2 CONT * '''Märta Knutsdotter.''' Married 1st to Halsten Petersson (Halsten Petersson's family). Married 2nd to the prefect of Norrvidinge Magnus Uddolfsson (Oxpanna)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halsten_Peterssons_%C3%A4tt Halsten Petersson's Family, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Halsten Petersson's family ,''' also called half lily , is a contemporary conventional name for a Swedish medieval squire family that took its name from the progenitor, knight and bailiff Halsten Petersson. The family died out 
2 CONC before Sweden's Riddarhus was founded in 1625, which is why it was never introduced there as nobility . The members of the family wore a red scotch, with half a golden lily laid in beams in the upper field.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''History'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Two land exchanges from 1377 and 1380 give good insight into the mutual kinship of several members.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family Tree'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Halsten Petersson, knight (1355), landowner and bailiff. His origin is unknown, but a (half) brother is mentioned, Arvid Petersson, who carried a spar in the coat of arms. 1336 and 1338 goods as thanks for faithful service. he w
2 CONC as given by King Magnus Eriksson but participated in King Erik Magnusson 's rebellion against his father, and is mentioned among Erik's five pledges in 1357, but is stated to have died on March 1, 1358. [ 3 ] '''Married Märta (Mar
2 CONC gareta) Knutsdotter ( Tre Rosor till Mörby ), daughter to Knut (Tre Rosor till Mörby) and Kristina Bengtsdotter in Haneström, daughter of the lawman in Västergötland Bengt Hafridsson .''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1- '''Johan Halstensson'''
2 CONT >>>1- '''Neck Johansson.''' According to Peder Månsson Utter (1566-1623) in ( Collectanea genealogica ), Halsten Johansson carried a fragmented shield with the upper half of a split (not split) lily gilt in the upper field. Accord
2 CONC ing to the same source, Halsten was the father of Håkan Halstensson. 
2 CONT >>>>>1- '''Håkan Halstensson,''' knight, named 1346-1380. [ 8 ] Married to Bengta, daughter of the knight and councilor Sigge Magnusson ( Vinstorpaätten , Håkan Tunesson's family ) and Ramborg. 
2 CONT >>>>>>>>'''NN Håkansdotter,''' married to Ulf Bengtsson ( Sparre of Hjulsta and Ängsö ), parents of, among others, Bishop Sigge in Strängnäs.
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>* 2 - '''Sven Jonsson (half lily) til Dinglevik,''' Steneby, died about 1484, was a gunsmith and signed up to Dingelvik , which was a salvation farm , later a manor in ( Steneby parish ), and married on 5 October 1449 [ 11 ] at
2 CONC  Stola with an Ingeborg Bytesdotter, the daughter of Tore Byting . 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>'''Three children are known:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* '''Ragnhild Svensdotter (half lily)
2 CONT >>>>* '''Karin Svensdotter (half lily)''' to Dinglevik, Steneby.'''
2 CONT >>>>* '''Botilla Svensdotter (half lily)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2 - '''Thord Halstensson'''
2 CONT * 3 - '''Knut Halstensson (half lily)''' was married to Katarina Guttormsdotter, daughter of Guttorm Toresson (split      shield) and Inga Gregersdotter ( Malstaätten )
2 CONT * 4 - '''Håkan Hallstensson''' During the civil war in 1364, had his estates confiscated by King Håkan Magnusson , which Håkan gave to Nils Bengtsson (Lion-faced, Bengt Nilsson's family)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =[https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000018049219838&photo_id=6000000206146828894&position=0 7407 1366 augusti 15, by the National Archives of Sweden]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Johan Knutsson (three roses) and Märta Knutsdotter announce that they ratify their aunt Ramfrid Bengtsdotter's last will, written in Swedish (to Julita Kloster), given on 18 May 1359.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Knutsson (three roses) and Märta Knutsdotter announce that they confirm their aunt Ramfrid Bengtsdotter's last, Swedish written will (to Julita Kloster), given on 18 May 1359 (SD 6092).
2 CONT
2 CONT Orig. on perg. (18.4 x 7.4 cm, fold 1.4 cm; 7 lines), with the monastery's letter number: 39 noted by Jonas Lorin at the extreme right of the fold, Sv. National sheet. (- R P B 724). It used to be attached to Mrs. Ramfrid's above-
2 CONC mentioned will (RPB 411).
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcripts in Hadorph's large copybook E 77-79, fol. 142 v (E 78, pag. 80), as well as (by . ) in Ürnhielm's Dipl. XI, pag. 724-725, bathing in Vitterhetsak: dep. in Sv. National sheet.
2 CONT Ala the thetta breff hera or see / helsom wi Joan knuzson oc maritts knuzdotir medh 'gudhi siælwme / kunnughum wi alom mannom at wara modhursystir itarsta 'testament som hoon giordhe ij sin liwandis tima wife ramfridh bendizdotir 
2 CONC stadfastom'wi medh thesso brewe oc sættium her fori was eghin insigle • oc thet testamentet er'scriwat aa swensko • oc byries swa / Ala thetta breff hora aller sea / iak etc.'* oc thet fernemda testament war giuit / anno domini •M
2 CONC  •CC°C • quinquagesimo nono die beati erici' regis et martiris / Date anno domini M• • CC°C• sexagesimo sexto die assumccionis virginis gloriose / One. No. 1, round, shows 3 five-petalled roses in a row obliquely across the shield
2 CONC . Paraphrase: + S' ION:KNVTES:S. No. 2, hexagonal, has M and the circumscription: MERTE:KNVTES ​​* D O T. . .
2 CONT
2 CONT • The word is found in Ramfrida testamente, SD 6092, with the same spelling and is apparently taken from there. Cf. SD 7424, note a.
