0 @N6000000002188118503@ NOTE Otto I, Landgrave of Hesse
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Otto I of Hesse (c. 1272, Marburg, Hessen-Nassau, Prussia–17 January 1328), Landgrave of Hesse.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was a son of Henry I, Landgrave of Hesse and his first wife Adelheid of Brunswick-Lunenburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family and children
1 CONT
1 CONT He was married 1297 in Saint Elisabethkirche, Marburg with Adelheid of Ravensburg, daughter of Count Otto III of Ravensberg and had the following children:
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Henry II the Iron (d. 3 June 1376, Kassel).
1 CONT    2. Otto (1301–1361, Wolmirstedt), Archbishop of Magdeburg.
1 CONT    3. Louis the Junker (d. 2 February 1345).
1 CONT    4. Hermann I the Elder (d. 1368/70).
1 CONT    5. Elisabeth (d. 30 May 1373), married before 8 May 1336 to Duke Rudolf II of Saxony.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Henry I Landgrave of Hesse
1 CONT 1308–1338 Succeeded by
1 CONT Henry II the Iron
