0 @N6000000003949821182@ NOTE He succeeded his father in 1112 as dom AFONSO I Conde de Portugal.  Ruling through his mother, he overthrew and expelled her from Portugal in 1128.  In 1135 he refused to swear homage to Alfonso VII King of Castile, from that time
1 CONC  using the title 'Prince of Portugal'.  He moved his capital to Coimbra.  In 1139 he won a notable victory against the Muslims in Santarem who were reduced to tributary status.  He proclaimed himseld dom AFONSO I "the Conqueror" K
1 CONC ing of Portugal in 1139.  His establishment of the archbishopric of Braga gave Portugal ecclesiastical independence.  He swore allegiance to the Pope[16].  He expanded his territory to the south, capturing Lisbon in 1147 with the 
1 CONC help of a force of English, French and Flemish crusaders[
