0 @N6000000007978029203@ NOTE Urraca, princess of Castile
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Urraca of Castile (1186 – 1220) was a daughter of Alfonso VIII of Castile and Leonora of England. Her maternal grandparents were Henry II of England and Eleanor of Aquitaine.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1208 Urraca married Afonso II of Portugal. They were the parents of five children.
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Sancho II (1207-1248)
1 CONT     * Afonso III (1210-1279)
1 CONT     * Leonor (1211- after 1231)
1 CONT     * Infante Fernando, Lord of Serpa (1217-1246)
1 CONT     * Vicente of Portugal (born & died 1219)
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Dulce Berenguer Queen consort of Portugal
1 CONT 1246-1248 Succeeded by
1 CONT Mécia Lopes de Haro
