0 @N6000000002188018950@ NOTE Canute V of Denmark
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Canute V of Denmark (Danish: Knud V Magnussen; born c. 1125 - August 9, 1157) was a King of Denmark and a co-regent with Sweyn III and Valdemar I between 1146 and 1157.
1 CONT
1 CONT Canute was the son of King Niels' son Magnus, who had slain Canute Lavard. After the abdication of Eric III in 1146, the magnates of Jutland declared him king and for the following years he tried in vain to defeat his rival Sweyn 
1 CONC III on Zealand. Canute participated in the 1147 Wendish Crusade. In 1151 he was expelled from Denmark and his request for help from Frederick Barbarossa only resulted in a compromise which made him the inferior co-regent of Sweyn.
1 CONT
1 CONT However, a secret co-operation with Valdemar, the son of Canute's father's old enemy, led to an 1154 alliance which made them sole rulers of the kingdom, forcing Sweyn to flee. After a new war, a final compromise in 1157 made Canu
1 CONC te the ruler of Zealand. During the peace banquet (the Bloodfeast of Roskilde) he was killed, allegedly by one of Sweyn's warriors.
1 CONT
1 CONT Nothing sure is known about his person and character. In 1156, he married Helena of Sweden. His half-sister Sofia of Minsk married Valdemar I, who avenged him the same year at the Battle of Grathe Heath by killing Sweyn.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT This article does not cite any references or sources. (January 2007)
1 CONT Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unverifiable material may be challenged and removed.
1 CONT Canute V
1 CONT Born: c. 1125 Died: August 9, 1157
1 CONT Regnal titles
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Eric Lamb King of Denmark
1 CONT 1146-1157
1 CONT with Sweyn Grathe &
1 CONT Valdemar the Great Succeeded by
1 CONT Valdemar the Great
0 @N6000000002187829077@ NOTE Wladyslaw III Spindleshanks
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Wladyslaw III Spindleshanks (Polish: Wladyslaw III Laskonogi; 1165? – 1231) was Duke of the province of Greater Poland and High Duke of all Poland, overlord of other Dukes, 1202-1206 and 1227-1228, during which periods he also was
1 CONC  Duke of Cracow, the duchy customarily held by the overlord.
1 CONT
1 CONT Wladyslaw became overlord of Poland in place of his cousin Leszek the White who was deposed. Wladyslaw then was himself deposed in favor of Leszek from the overlordship. Only after twenty years, and a couple of reigns in between, 
1 CONC he succeeded to get restored.
1 CONT
1 CONT Wladyslaw was the son of Mieszko III the Old and his successor in their family part-realm of Greater Poland.
0 @N6000000004533118775@ NOTE <b>Sunesen, Ebbe,</b> o. 1158-1208, sjællandsk Stormand,
1 CONT en af de ældste Sunesønner, fik efter sin Fader, Sune Ebbesen (IV,397),
1 CONT Gaarden Knardrup i Nordsjælland, hvortil der hørte meget andet
1 CONT Gods; saaledes havde E. S. Ejendomme i Herlev, som han
1 CONT skjænkede til Esrom Kloster, og i Alsønderup ved Arresø. Han stod i
1 CONT Venskabsforhold til Abbed Vilhelm i Æbelholt, og denne priser i
1 CONT høje Toner E. S.s Ædelhed og Fromhed, men maatte dog en
1 CONT Gang klage over hans Fogeds Overgreb. E. S. hørte til Danmarks
1 CONT anseteste Mænd. Kong Knud lod ham og hans Broder Anders
1 CONT mægle i en Fiskeristrid mellem Æbelholt Kloster og Kronens
1 CONT Landboer og paa Borgen Grønholt 1196 bevidne Stadfæstelsen af
1 CONT Uommen mellem Cistercienserne i Guldholm og Cluniacenserne ved
1 CONT Slesvig, og ligesom de andre Sunesønner (undtagen Jacob) hørte
1 CONT han til det fornemme Broderskab, som i denne Konges Tid var
1 CONT udbredt over hele Landet. En Datter af E. S., Benedicte, blev
1 CONT endog Sveriges Dronning, i det Kong Sverker II, som var opfostret
1 CONT i Danmark, kaarede hende til Brud; hun døde for øvrigt tidlig
1 CONT efter at have født en Datter. Baandet mellem Sverker og hans
1 CONT Svigerfader brast dog ikke, og hans Herredømme opretholdtes
1 CONT længe, sikkert ved Støtte fra dansk Side. Endelig lykkedes det
1 CONT hans Medbejler, Erik Knutsson, at fordrive ham, og Sverker tyede
1 CONT til Danmark, hvor E. S. og hans Brødre rustede en Hær for at
1 CONT hjælpe ham. Man trængte frem i Vestergøtland, og ved Lena
1 CONT kom det til en haard Kamp (31. Jan. 1208), der endte med
1 CONT Nederlag for Sverker, og blandt de faldne vare E. S. og hans Broder
1 CONT Laurens; 2 Aar efter gjorde Sverker et nyt Forsøg paa at
1 CONT gjenvinde sit Rige, men faldt i Slaget ved Gestilren. Skjønt
1 CONT Sunesønnernes Tog til Sverige næppe har været et dansk
1 CONT Rigsforetagende, var Indtrykket ved den stolte Æts Nederlag dog ikke
1 CONT mindre overvældende; man mindedes det i en tungsindig Folkevise.
1 CONT E. S. og Laurens bleve jordfæstede i Sorø Klosterkirke; begge havde
1 CONT de været Klosterets Velgjørere. Af E. S.s Sønner blev Johannes
1 CONT (d. 1232) Marsk, Peder (d. 1256) arvede Knardrup og havde en Strid
1 CONT med Erik Plovpenning; af de 4 Døtre ægtede Cæcilie Jon
1 CONT Reinmothsen og blev ved ham Moder til Jon Litle (X, 343), en anden
1 CONT var gift med en tysk Grev Engelbert, hvem Folkevisen om
1 CONT Lenaslaget berømmer.
1 CONT
1 CONT <i>Hans Olrik.</i>
