1 CONT HENRY OF ENGLAND (styled "the Young King"), born at Bermondsey, Surrey 28 Feb. 1155, Duke of Normandy, Count of Anjou and Maine, crowned joint King of England 14 June 1170.  He married at Neubourg in Normandy 2 Nov. 1160 MARGARET 
1 CONC ... OF FRANCE. ... They had one son, William, born 19 June 1177, died in a few days.  He was recrowned together with his queen in 1172.  He rebelled in 1173-74 and again in 1183.  HENRY OF ENGLAND, joint King of England (with his 
1 CONC father), died at Château Martel in Touraine 11 June 1183, and was buried in Rouen Cathedral.  His widow, Margaret, married (2nd) shortly after 24 August 1186 (as his 4th wife) Bela III, King of Hungary. ... They had no issue.  Bel
1 CONC a III, King of Hungary, died 23 April 1196, and was buried at Székesfehervar.  Following her husband Bela III's death, Margaret made a pilgrimage to the Holy Land.  She died at Acre shortly after 10 Sept. 1197.
