1 CONC he Marshall - E arl of Pembrook.  Once crowed King in May 1199, John proved initially to be a gifted administrator, showing concern for his kingdom.  He di d exhibit a growing distrust of the Norman barons once he became King .  D
1 CONC uring John's reign, the exchequer, Chancery and law courts began t o function more efficiently.  Many of the problems of his reign arose due to bad luck.  Upon his arrival in England, he promoted Huber Walte r to the office of Cha
